      "narrative": "AheadComputing is a Seed-stage chip design company that has raised $51.5M to date. Valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 3 public semiconductor names (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private peers in the same sector, with particular focus on 3 recent Series A financings: SambaNova Systems ($11.0B), Rebellions ($2.3B), and d-Matrix ($2.0B).\n\nTwo methods prove applicable. Stage-progression analysis uses the $52M raised as a valuation proxy and applies a typical 2.5x step-up multiplier from Seed to next stage, yielding $129M. Peer-median analysis anchors to the median valuation of the 3 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables at $2.3B, with the range spanning $2.0B to $11.0B. Public-comp anchoring via price-to-sales cannot be applied: the public semiconductors median trades at 20.5x sales, but AheadComputing's revenue is not disclosed, preventing multiples-based valuation.\n\nThe triangulated range spans $109M (low) to $2.7B (high), with a median of $1.2B. The wide spread reflects the gap between stage-based and peer-based methods. Key uncertainties center on technology differentiation versus peers, path to revenue, and whether recent Series A valuations in the space represent sustainable market pricing or cyclical peaks.",
