      "narrative": "Aurora Innovation is a public-stage autonomous systems company in the Drones & Autonomous sector, founded by Chris Urmson, Sterling Anderson, and Drew Bagnell. The company has raised $2.0B to date. The relevant peer universe consists of eight private companies in the same sector, including Joby Aviation, Archer Aviation, Waymo, Wayve, and Zipline, with no direct public comparables available.\n\nThe Peer-Median method is not applicable to this valuation. The Drones & Autonomous sector contains only seven same-sector peers total. When filtered for stage alignment, adjacent-stage proximity, or similar valuation tier, no subset reaches the minimum three-datapoint threshold required for reliable median analysis. Relying on an all-sector median would introduce significant distortion given the heterogeneity of business models, commercialization timelines, and technology risk profiles across the broader autonomous systems landscape.\n\nThe absence of a sufficiently deep peer cohort and the lack of public trading comparables presents a material constraint on quantitative triangulation. A credible valuation would require alternative methodologies\u2014such as venture-backed precedent transaction analysis of the identified private peers, or DCF modeling anchored to commercialization milestones and capital intensity assumptions\u2014alongside explicit articulation of the key uncertainties: path to profitability, regulatory clearance timelines, and capital requirements through scale.",
