      "narrative": "SendCutSend, a Series A robotics and manufacturing company, has raised approximately $110M to date. The valuation analysis draws on two primary methods triangulated against a peer universe of nine companies\u2014one public and eight private\u2014primarily operating in robotics and adjacent automation sectors.\n\nStage-progression analysis applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier to the $110M total raised proxy, implying a $220M valuation. Peer-median analysis examines four same-sector comparables spanning Series B and Seed stages, yielding a median valuation of $1.7B with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B. The peer set includes Generalist AI ($2.0B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B), Dexterity ($1.6B), and Walden Robotics ($1.1B), all operating in manufacturing automation and robotics.\n\nTriangulation of both methods produces a valuation range of $187M (low) to $2.0B (high), with a median estimate of $960M. The wide spread reflects material stage and maturity differences within the peer set; the stage-progression method anchors conservatively to capital deployed, while peer comps span both earlier and later stage companies. Key uncertainties include SendCutSend's relative market position and growth trajectory relative to Series B-stage peers commanding valuations near or above $1.6B, and the applicability of seed-stage comparables (Walden at $1.1B) given SendCutSend's more advanced funding position.",
