      "narrative": "Farcast is a Series A-stage space and aerospace company founded by Siamak Ebadi that has raised $23.6M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 13 comparable companies: 5 public tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private firms including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, ICEYE, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs.\n\nTwo triangulation methods prove applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, yielding $47M. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector comparables at equivalent or adjacent stage\u2014Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B), Aalyria ($1.3B), and Starcloud ($1.1B)\u2014produces a $1.3B median with a $1.1B\u2013$2.0B range. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied; the six-ticker Space & Aerospace sector median P/S of 27.4x requires revenue disclosure unavailable for private companies.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $40M\u2013$1.5B, with a median of $674M across the two applicable methods. The wide spread reflects material tension between early-stage funding history ($47M floor) and peer comparable valuations dominated by more mature capital-stage businesses. Key uncertainties include Farcast's revenue trajectory, technical differentiation relative to the peer set, and capital requirements for the next funding milestone. Additional clarity on unit economics and commercialization timeline would narrow this range materially.",
