      "narrative": "Impossible Metals, a seed-stage company in Climate & Energy, has raised $15M to date. The sector peer universe comprises one public company and eight private competitors including Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Enovix. The founding team brings relevant domain expertise: Oliver Gunasekara (30+ years in tech, prior leadership at ARM), Jason Gillham (subsea robotics, founded 2G Robotics with subsequent acquisition by Voyis in January 2020), and Renee Grogan (sustainability and extractive resources background).\n\nGiven the nascent stage and lack of sufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables within the Climate & Energy sector, a peer-median approach was not applicable. The stage-progression method, however, applies a standard 2.5x multiplier from seed to next-stage funding benchmarks, yielding an implied valuation of $38M based on the $15M raised proxy. This methodology reflects typical venture progression stepping without reliance on sparse peer data.\n\nThe analysis triangulates to a valuation range of $32M to $43M, with a median of $38M. This range is derived from a single applicable method and should be treated with corresponding caution. Primary uncertainties include subsea resource extraction regulatory risk, capital intensity of commercialization, and technology validation relative to incumbent operators. The narrow methodological foundation underscores the need for updated inputs as the company progresses toward Series A and competitive positioning clarifies.",
