      "narrative": "Reditus Space is a seed-stage space and aerospace company founded by Stef Crum (CEO, PhD in Space Systems Engineering with prior NASA and Space Force orbital operations and reentry experience) and Will Sherman (CTO). The company has raised $7.1M to date. The valuation universe consists of 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers in Space & Aerospace, including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, ICEYE, and Sierra Space.\n\nOnly one valuation method proved applicable given data constraints. Stage-progression analysis uses the $7.1M total raised as a proxy for seed-stage value and applies a typical 2.5x multiplier to the next financing stage, yielding an implied valuation of $18M. Peer-median analysis was not viable; while 14 same-sector peers exist, insufficient datapoints met narrow filtering criteria (same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar valuation tier). Public-comp anchoring could not be applied because the target's revenue is not disclosed, precluding meaningful price-to-sales multiples despite a sector median of 27.4x across five public tickers.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $15M to $20M, with a median point of $18M. This range reflects a 2.1x to 2.8x step-up from capital deployed. Key uncertainties include the absence of comparable private-company data within the narrow seed-stage cohort and lack of revenue or profitability metrics. The valuation should be stress-tested against the company's product maturity, customer traction, and unit economics once available.",
