      "narrative": "Monarch Quantum is a Growth-stage quantum computing company led by Dr. Timothy Day (former founder of Daylight Solutions, acquired by Leonardo DRS in 2017) and a team including CTO Michael Pushkarsky and President/CFO Bryan Taylor. The company has raised $115M+ in capital and contracts. The quantum computing sector includes 3 public peers (IONQ, RGTI, QBTS) and 8 private competitors including Quantinuum, IonQ, PsiQuantum, D-Wave Quantum, and SandboxAQ.\n\nA Stage-Progression methodology is applicable here, using the $115M total raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 1.2x step-up multiplier typical of Growth-stage advancement, yielding $138M. Peer-Median triangulation is not applicable due to insufficient same-stage and adjacent-stage comparables within the Quantum Computing sector\u2014while 8 private peers exist, none meet the narrow filtering criteria of matching stage and valuation tier, making a median calculation misleading.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $117M (low) to $159M (median $138M), anchored solely on stage-progression methodology. Key uncertainties include the absence of comparable-company validation within Monarch's specific stage and tier; reliance on a single method limits confidence in the range. The wide spread ($42M across the range) reflects this single-method dependency. Revenue multiples, customer concentration, and IP portfolio strength remain unquantified drivers of final valuation.",
