      "narrative": "Spaceium is a seed-stage space & aerospace company founded by orbital mechanics and propulsion specialists with NASA and legacy rocket-engine experience. The company has raised $6.3M to date. The Space & Aerospace sector includes 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers spanning multiple maturity stages, though few direct seed-stage analogues exist.\n\nGiven the limited seed-stage peer set in this sector, only the stage-progression method is reliably applicable. Using total capital raised ($6.3M) as a proxy for seed-stage valuation and applying a typical 2.5x step-up multiplier to the next funding stage yields an implied valuation of $15.75M. Public comps in Space & Aerospace trade at a median 27.4x revenue, but without disclosed target revenue, this anchor cannot be calibrated. Peer-median analysis is inapplicable due to insufficient same-stage and adjacent-stage comparables meeting filter thresholds.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $13M to $18M, with a median point estimate of $16M. This range reflects the stage-progression method alone and carries meaningful uncertainty. Key dependencies include (1) the applicability of the 2.5x multiplier to this specific founder profile and market opportunity, and (2) the absence of revenue and unit economics data, which would refine any revenue-multiple valuation. The range should be stress-tested against sector-specific risk factors and capital efficiency benchmarks as additional financial data becomes available.",
