      "narrative": "Diraq is a Series A quantum computing company that has raised $100M+, founded by Andrew Dzurak. The quantum computing sector comprises a peer universe of 3 public companies (IONQ, RGTI, QBTS) and 8 private firms including Quantinuum, IonQ, PsiQuantum, D-Wave Quantum, and SandboxAQ.\n\nStage-progression methodology is applicable to Diraq's valuation. Using the $100M total capital raised as a base proxy and applying a typical 2.0x step-up multiplier for progression through Series A, this method implies a valuation of $200M. A peer-median approach cannot be reliably applied due to insufficient comparable data points at the same stage and valuation tier within quantum computing; while 8 same-sector peers exist, none of the narrow filters (same-stage, adjacent-stage, similar valuation tier) yielded the minimum three datapoints needed to support a robust median.\n\nThe quantified triangulation yields a range of $170M (low) to $230M (high), with a median of $200M. This analysis is constrained by single-method reliance; the primary uncertainty stems from the sparse peer dataset within quantum computing at Diraq's stage, limiting cross-validation. The $200M median represents the most supported estimate given available data, though the range width reflects material uncertainty around comparable precedent in the sector.",
