      "narrative": "Phoenix Tailings is a Series B climate and energy technology company that has raised $117.8M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private companies\u2014KoBold Metals (Series C, $3.0B), Electric Hydrogen (Series C, $1.0B), and Amogy (Series C, $700M)\u2014alongside one public comparable and eight additional private benchmarks in the broader climate-tech ecosystem.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total capital raised as a proxy valuation baseline, applies a 1.9x Series B step-up multiplier to the $118M raised figure, yielding $224M. Peer-median analysis across the three same-sector comparables produces a $1.0B median valuation, with a range spanning $700M to $3.0B. The peer-median approach reflects meaningful dispersion driven by differences in technology maturity, capital intensity, and market positioning within the climate-tech sector.\n\nThe triangulated range is $190M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $612M. The wide band reflects the inherent challenge of valuing Series B companies relative to Series C peers without intervening funding data. Key uncertainties include the degree to which Phoenix Tailings' technology and market application align with the sampled comparables, and whether near-term financing activity will narrow stage-specific multiples or shift the peer median.",
