      "narrative": "Saronic is a Series D-stage defense and security company founded by Dino Mavrookas, Rob Lehman, Vibhav Altekar, and Doug Lambert, currently valued at $9.25B on $2.6B+ in cumulative capital raised. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of 10 comparable companies\u20142 public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms spanning the same sector and stage, including Helsing, Chaos Industries, and Onebrief.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using the $4.0B last post-money valuation and applying a typical 1.5x Series D step-up multiplier, implies a value of $6.0B. Peer-median analysis across three same-stage, same-sector comparables (Helsing at $18.0B, Chaos Industries at $4.5B, and Onebrief at $2.1B) yields a median of $4.5B, with a range spanning $2.1B to $18.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis across both methods supports a valuation range of $3.8B to $6.9B, with a median of $5.2B. The current $9.25B valuation sits materially above this derived range. Key uncertainties include the wide dispersion in peer valuations (6.8x spread from min to max) and the stage-progression method's reliance on typical step-up multipliers that may not reflect sector-specific momentum or company-specific fundamentals. Resolution of these gaps requires examination of revenue multiples, growth rates, and market positioning relative to the peer cohort.",
