      "narrative": "Andrenam is a Series A-stage defense and security company founded by Matej Cernosek and Alex Chu that has raised $18M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 4 same-sector, same-stage private companies (Stark Defence, Castelion, Singularity, NODA AI) ranging from $125M to $4.0B, supplemented by 2 public defense peers and 8 additional private comparables including Anduril Industries.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applied. Stage-progression applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement to the $18M raised proxy, implying $36M. Peer-median methodology uses the median valuation of the 4 directly comparable companies at $700M, reflecting the spread across the cohort (min $125M, max $4.0B). These approaches produce material dispersion, reflecting the inherent volatility in early-stage defense-tech valuations.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $31M (low) to $805M (high), with a median of $368M. The wide spread reflects two distinct narratives: the stage-progression method anchors near the capital deployed, while the peer-median approach incorporates the elevated multiples observed across the Defense & Security peer set. Key uncertainties include revenue traction relative to peer cohorts, the maturity and defensibility of core IP, and customer concentration among government and quasi-government buyers. Without visibility into Andrenam's current revenue and unit economics relative to named comparables, the $368M median should be treated as indicative only.",
