      "narrative": "Reflect Orbital is a Series A space and aerospace company that has raised $35.2M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of 3 private companies at the same or adjacent stage (Cowboy Space Corporation at $2.0B, Aalyria at $1.3B, and Starcloud at $1.1B), as well as a broader public market anchor of 5 traded Space & Aerospace names (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) with a median P/S multiple of 27.4x.\n\nTwo methods prove applicable. Stage-progression anchors on the $35M raised as a proxy valuation floor and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, implying $70M. Peer-median valuation uses the three private comparables in Space & Aerospace at same or adjacent stage, yielding a $1.3B median with a $1.1B\u2013$2.0B range. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied without revenue disclosure from Reflect Orbital. The two applicable methods triangulate to a range of $60M (low) to $1.5B (high) with a median of $685M.\n\nThe wide spread reflects genuine uncertainty in stage positioning and relative maturity versus peers. The peer-median method's $1.3B result rests on limited sample size (3 companies) spanning heterogeneous stages. Stage-progression offers a more conservative floor based on capital deployed. Key uncertainties include technology differentiation, capital efficiency, and path to commercial revenue relative to the peer set.",
