      "narrative": "Relativity Space is a private-stage space and aerospace company founded by Tim Ellis and Jordan Noone that has raised $1.335B to date. The valuation universe comprises 5 public comps (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, Impulse Space, ICEYE, and Sierra Space.\n\nStandard triangulation methods yield limited conclusions. Peer-median valuation is inapplicable: while 14 same-sector private peers exist, fewer than 3 satisfy narrow filters for stage, adjacency, or valuation tier\u2014the threshold required for statistical reliability. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples cannot be applied because Relativity Space's revenue is not disclosed; the broader Space & Aerospace public universe trades at a 27.4x sector median P/S across the 5 identified tickers, but without target revenue this multiple is uninformative.\n\nThe analysis supports no quantitative valuation range at this time. Material constraints include: absence of disclosed revenue, insufficient same-stage private comparables with disclosed valuations, and the extreme heterogeneity within aerospace (launch services, satellite imaging, on-orbit manufacturing all trade on fundamentally different models). Forward valuation work would require either disclosure of Relativity's revenue and margin profile, or sourcing recent transaction data from the identified peer set. The $1.335B raised provides a floor on investor appetite but does not establish fair value absent performance metrics.",
