      "narrative": "Impulse Space, a private-stage space and aerospace company founded by Tom Mueller, is valued at $4.26B following $525M in total capital raised. The valuation assessment draws on a comparable universe of 10 same-sector peers spanning similar valuation tiers, including both public equities (Rocket Lab, Planet Labs, Firefly Aerospace) and late-stage private companies (ICEYE at $12.0B, Sierra Space at $8.0B).\n\nThe peer-median method is the applicable triangulation approach. The median valuation across the 10-company peer set is $2.1B, with a range of $1.1B to $12.0B. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiple (median 27.4x across six public space-sector tickers) cannot be applied due to absence of revenue disclosure. This is standard for private companies at Impulse's stage.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $1.8B to $2.5B, centered on the peer median of $2.1B. The current $4.26B valuation sits materially above this range, reflecting either a significant financing round premium not yet reflected in comparable data or a differentiated market position relative to the peer set. Key uncertainties include Impulse's revenue trajectory (undisclosed), customer concentration, and relative technology positioning within a rapidly consolidating sector. Confidence in the $2.1B implied value is constrained by sample heterogeneity and limited visibility into private peer fundamentals.",
