      "narrative": "Astranis, a Series E space and aerospace company, has raised $1.2B+ to date. The valuation analysis relies on a peer universe of three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private companies (ICEYE at $12.0B Series F, Apex Space at $2.3B Series D, and Varda Space Industries at $1.6B Series D), supplemented by reference to five publicly traded Space & Aerospace comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) trading at a median EV/Sales multiple of 27.4x.\n\nTwo methods produce quantifiable results. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.4x step-up multiplier to Astranis's last known post-money valuation of $3.5B, yielding $4.9B. Peer-median valuation across the three private comparables generates $2.3B, with a reported range of $1.6B to $12.0B. Public-comparable anchoring cannot be applied absent disclosed revenue figures, which private companies typically withhold.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $2.0B to $5.6B, with a median of $3.6B across the two applicable methods. This range reflects material uncertainty: peer dispersion spans an order of magnitude, driven partly by stage heterogeneity (Series D vs. Series F). Key sensitivities include capital intensity trends within satellite/space infrastructure, near-term revenue visibility, and whether Astranis's customer concentration and regulatory dependencies narrow relative to public-market analogues.",
