      "narrative": "Viridian Space is a pre-seed-stage company in the Space & Aerospace sector that has raised $2M+. The valuation universe includes 5 public comps (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, ICEYE, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs.\n\nThe Stage-Progression method is the applicable triangulation approach. Using total capital raised ($2M) as a proxy for pre-seed valuation and applying a 2.5x multiplier typical of pre-seed to next-stage advancement yields an implied valuation of $5M. The Peer-Median method could not be applied due to insufficient comparable datapoints at identical or adjacent stage and tier within the narrow space sector cohort\u2014only 0 same-stage and 1 adjacent-stage comparable were identified. Public-Comp Anchoring was not applicable because the target company's revenue is not disclosed, precluding use of the 27.4x median price-to-sales multiple observed across the 5 public Space & Aerospace peers.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $4M to $6M, with a median of $5M. This single-method triangulation carries material uncertainty: the range reflects reasonable sensitivity around stage-typical step-up multiers rather than cross-validated triangulation. Key risks include the early-stage nature of the company and the thin comparable set for pre-seed space ventures. Revenue generation, technical milestones, and capital efficiency will be critical determinants of next-round valuation progression.",
