      "narrative": "Firefly Aerospace is a public-stage Space & Aerospace company founded by Tom Markusic, currently valued at approximately $2.9B following an $868M IPO. The valuation analysis draws from a peer universe of 3 same-sector, same-stage public comparables: Rocket Lab ($40.0B), Planet Labs ($7.6B), and Astroscale ($840M).\n\nThe peer-median method is the applicable triangulation approach given available data. The median valuation across these three public peers is $7.6B, with a wide dispersion ranging from $840M at the low end to $40.0B at the high end. This reflects material heterogeneity in the Space & Aerospace public market, where scale and stage of commercialization vary significantly. A public-comp anchoring method using the sector's median P/S multiple of 27.4x across 6 public tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) cannot be applied without Firefly's reported revenue, which is not available on file.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range derived from this single applicable method is $6.4B (low), $7.6B (median), and $8.7B (high). The current trading valuation of $2.9B sits substantially below this peer-derived range. Key uncertainties include revenue visibility, the durability of near-term Space & Aerospace multiples, and whether Firefly's asset base and contract pipeline justify positioning relative to higher-valued peers or closer to the Astroscale end of the comparables spectrum.",
