      "narrative": "Hadrian is a Series D robotics and manufacturing company seeking valuation at its $1.6B last post-money. The analysis draws on a peer universe of nine comparable companies\u2014one public (277810.KQ) and eight private\u2014including same-stage peers Exotec ($2.0B) and Divergent ($2.3B, Series E), as well as earlier-stage benchmarks Agile Robots and Nimble Robotics (both $1.0B, Series C).\n\nTwo methods triangulate the valuation. Stage-progression modeling, applying a typical 1.5x multiplier to the $1.6B base, implies $2.4B. Peer-median analysis across four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yields $1.5B (range: $1.0B\u2013$2.3B), capturing the broader dispersion in the robotics sector. The median implied value across methods is $1.9B.\n\nThe triangulated range is $1.3B to $2.8B, with the midpoint at $1.9B. Hadrian's current valuation sits near the lower quartile of this range, reflecting either valuation conservatism or sector-wide uncertainty. Key drivers of range width include heterogeneity in peer stage progression and divergent funding multiples within early-stage robotics. Capital efficiency and path to revenue remain critical unknowns that would narrow this band materially.",
