      "narrative": "Salient Motion is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $12M to date. The valuation analysis triangulates across a competitive set of 9 private and 1 public comparable company, primarily robotics and manufacturing players at Series A and Series B stages, including Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, Generalist AI, and Walden Robotics.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using the $12M total raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, implies a $24M valuation. Peer-median analysis across four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yielded a median valuation of $1.7B, with a range spanning $1.1B (Walden Robotics, Seed) to $2.0B (Generalist AI, Series B).\n\nThe wide gap between these methods\u2014$24M versus $1.7B\u2014reflects the fundamental disparity between early-stage financing multiples and later-stage peer valuations. A reconciled range of $20M (low) to $2.0B (high), with a median of $862M, is supported by the data. The primary uncertainty is whether peer multiples apply appropriately given Salient Motion's earlier stage and smaller scale relative to Series B-funded competitors. Stage-progression alone suggests a more conservative $20\u2013$24M range; peer comparables imply substantially higher value if the company achieves comparable milestones. Capital efficiency and revenue traction remain critical discriminators.",
