      "narrative": "Terraform Industries is a Series A climate and energy company founded by Casey Handmer that has raised $26M to date. The valuation benchmark set includes one public comparable (LNZA) and eight private peers in the Climate & Energy sector, including Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Enovix. However, the private peer set lacks sufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage companies with comparable valuation tiers to support a reliable peer-median approach.\n\nGiven data constraints, stage-progression methodology is the primary applicable technique. Using total capital raised as a proxy valuation floor and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to later-stage advancement yields an implied valuation of $52M. This reflects the assumption that investors price subsequent rounds at approximately double the prior stage's entry point, holding for companies with materially de-risked technical or commercial milestones between rounds.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $44M to $60M, with a median point of $52M. The range width reflects uncertainty around (1) stage-progression multiplier applicability for early-stage frontier tech, where capital efficiency and burn rate vary significantly, and (2) the absence of granular peer transaction data. Key variables materially affecting valuation include technology validation progress, pathway to unit economics, and capital requirements to reach Series B milestones. Additional data on comparable recent Series A closings in frontier energy would sharpen this estimate.",
