      "narrative": "Joby Aviation, a publicly traded player in the Drones & Autonomous sector, is evaluated here against a peer set of four same-sector comparable companies spanning Series D through public stages. The universe includes both private (Wayve at $8.6B Series D, Zipline at $7.6B Series G, Nuro at $6.0B Series G) and public (Archer Aviation at $3.3B) references, establishing a valuation range floor at $3.3B and ceiling at $8.6B.\n\nPeer-median triangulation, the applicable method given available data, yields $6.8B based on the four-company sample. This method directly anchors to observed market valuations for functionally similar-stage autonomous vehicle and logistics platforms. The median aligns closely with Joby's current public market capitalization of $6.86B, suggesting the equity market is pricing the company in line with peer risk-return profiles in this sector.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range supports $5.8B to $7.8B, with a median of $6.8B. This narrow band reflects limited methodological diversity\u2014only peer comparison is applicable with the provided data\u2014and does not incorporate revenue multiples, DCF assumptions, or venture-stage discount rates. Key uncertainties include the timing and regulatory pathway to commercialization for eVTOL aircraft, which fundamentally drives optionality value across this peer set but cannot be quantified from current inputs.",
