      "narrative": "Etched is a Series E chip design company that has raised $800M to date and carries a current post-money valuation of $5.0B. The valuation assessment draws on a universe of 8 private peers in Chips & Semiconductors and 3 public comparables (ALAB, NVDA, AMD), though the public anchor cannot be applied due to absence of disclosed revenue.\n\nTwo methods triangulate the fair value range. Stage-progression analysis applies a typical 1.4x step-up multiplier to the $5.0B last post-money, yielding $7.0B. Peer-median analysis across 8 same-sector companies yields $2.3B, with the peer cohort ranging from $1.0B (low) to $11.0B (high) and including Ayar Labs at $3.8B and Tenstorrent at $2.7B. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (median 20.5x across semiconductors) cannot be applied without disclosed revenue figures.\n\nThe triangulated valuation supports a range of $2.0B to $8.0B with a median of $4.7B. The current $5.0B valuation sits near the median and above the peer median of $2.3B, consistent with Etched's later stage and capital raise. Key uncertainties include the absence of revenue disclosure (preventing P/S-based validation), stage-specific step-up assumptions, and the heterogeneity within the peer set\u2014particularly wide dispersal driven by SambaNova's $11.0B Series A outlier.",
