      "narrative": "Extropic is a Series A-stage semiconductor company founded by Guillaume Verdon and Trevor McCourt, having raised $50M+. Valuation analysis draws from a universe of 8 private and 3 public semiconductor comparables, with same-stage private peers including SambaNova Systems, Rebellions, and d-Matrix.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis uses the $50M total raised as a proxy baseline and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A advancement, implying a $100M valuation. Peer-median analysis compares Extropic against three same-sector, same-stage private companies with a median valuation of $2.3B and a range of $2.0B to $11.0B. Public-comp anchoring using semiconductor multiples (median 20.5x P/S across ALAB, NVDA, AMD) cannot be applied without the target's revenue, which private companies typically do not disclose.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a range of $85M to $2.7B, with a median of $1.2B across both applicable methods. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty: stage-progression suggests a conservative floor near the capital-raised proxy, while peer-median is heavily influenced by outlier SambaNova at $11.0B. The valuation range hinges critically on technology differentiation, path to meaningful revenue, and whether Extropic's technical positioning merits positioning at the peer median or toward the lower quartile of the semiconductor Series A universe.",
