      "narrative": "Cover is a Series B-stage housing and construction company founded by Alexis Rivas and Jemuel Joseph that has raised $100M+. The comp universe consists of four private peers in the housing and construction sector\u2014Plantd Materials, Cuby Technologies, Somos, and Charge Robotics\u2014with no public comparables available for direct benchmarking.\n\nThe valuation analysis applies a stage-progression methodology, which is applicable given Cover's clear Series B position. Using total capital raised of $100M as a baseline proxy, a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement yields an implied valuation of $190M. This single-method approach produces a triangulated range of $162M (low) to $218M (high), centered at a median of $190M.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $162M\u2013$218M, with $190M as the central estimate. Key uncertainties center on the limited comp set of private peers and the absence of public market data; a single methodological approach reduces triangulation robustness. The stage-progression method assumes typical venture progression dynamics, which may not capture Cover-specific unit economics, market position, or capital efficiency relative to housing and construction sector norms. Additional data on revenue multiples, growth rates, or proceeds from recent fundraising would strengthen conviction in this range.",
