      "narrative": "Auterion is a Series B defense and security software company founded by Lorenz Meier and Kevin Sartori. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 10 peers\u20142 public companies (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms in the same sector and stage. The private peer set includes Dream Security, Harmattan AI, Code Metal, Defense Unicorns, and Heven AeroTech, among others.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, anchoring to Auterion's $130M in total capital raised, applies a typical Series B forward step-up multiplier of 1.9x, yielding $247M. Peer-median analysis across the 6 same-stage, same-sector comparables yields a median valuation of $1.1B, with a range spanning $300M (low) to $3.0B (high). The peer set reflects material dispersion, reflective of differentiation in revenue scale, technology maturity, or customer concentration within the defense tech subsector.\n\nTriangulating these two methods produces a valuation range of $210M (low) to $1.3B (high), with a median indication of $686M. The wide spread reflects tension between Auterion's modest capital history relative to peer medians, and the elevated multiples observed among more mature Series B defense tech companies. Key uncertainties include revenue run-rate, customer concentration among government versus commercial buyers, and whether peers' valuations reflect recent market repricing in defense tech.",
