      "narrative": "Firehawk Aerospace is a Series A-stage defense & security company founded by Will Edwards, having raised $25M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 10 peers\u20142 public companies (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms including Stark Defence, Castelion, Singularity, and NODA AI, all operating in the same sector and stage.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $25M raised as a valuation proxy and applies a 2.0x multiplier typical for Series A step-ups, implying a $50M valuation. Peer-median analysis across the four same-sector, same-stage comparables yields a median valuation of $700M, derived from a range spanning $125M (NODA AI) to $4.0B (Stark Defence). The peer cohort exhibits significant dispersion, reflecting heterogeneity in market position and maturity within the Series A defense technology segment.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $42.5M to $805M, with a median point estimate of $375M. The wide band reflects fundamental tension between stage-implied fundamentals ($50M) and peer-market pricing ($700M median). Key uncertainties include Firehawk's relative differentiation within the peer set, the scalability of its defense applications, and customer concentration risk\u2014factors that would move the valuation toward either the lower or upper bound of the range.",
