      "narrative": "Galvanick is a Series E-stage company in Defense & Security that has raised $10M+ to date. The valuation analysis relies on a peer-median approach, given that stage-progression methodology proved unreliable due to inconsistent base-value inputs. The applicable comp universe comprises five same-sector, same/adjacent-stage peers: Helsing ($18.0B, Series D), Saronic ($9.2B, Series D), Chaos Industries ($4.5B, Series D), Skydio ($4.4B, Series F), and Onebrief ($2.1B, Series D). This peer set is drawn from a broader universe of 10 companies (2 public, 8 private), including established names such as Anduril Industries, Shield AI, and Quantum-Systems.\n\nThe peer-median method yields a valuation of $4.5B, with the five-company sample ranging from $2.1B to $18.0B. This wide spread reflects material variance in the Defense & Security frontier-tech segment, likely driven by differences in revenue traction, technology maturity, and customer concentration. Triangulation across the available method produces a central estimate of $4.5B, with a low estimate of $3.8B (15% haircut to median) and high estimate of $5.2B (15% premium).\n\nKey uncertainties include Galvanick's revenue and growth rate relative to peers, customer concentration risk, and technology differentiation within the crowded autonomous systems and AI-for-defense subsector. Without revenue or profitability data, this estimate carries material estimation error.",
