      "narrative": "Distributed Spectrum is a Seed-stage Defense & Security company that has raised $25M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of five same-sector, same/adjacent-stage companies\u2014including UFORCE (Seed, $1.0B), Stark Defence (Series A, $4.0B), Castelion (Series A, $1.0B), Singularity (Series A, $400M), and NODA AI (Series A, $125M)\u2014alongside broader public comparables in the sector.\n\nTwo methods triangulate valuation. The Stage-Progression method applies a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage advancement, yielding $62M based on the $25M raised proxy. The Peer-Median method benchmarks against the five-company cohort, which exhibits a median valuation of $1.0B with a range spanning $125M to $4.0B, reflecting substantial dispersion in the sector. This second method implies $1.0B.\n\nThe triangulation supports a valuation range of $53M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $531M. The 20x spread between low and high estimates reflects meaningful uncertainty: the Stage-Progression method anchors conservatively to recent capital, while the Peer-Median method is heavily influenced by outliers such as Stark Defence's $4.0B valuation and the $1.0B UFORCE comparable. Stage progression relative to peer funding and product maturity remains the primary source of variance in this analysis.",
