      "narrative": "Darkhive, a Series A-stage defense and security company founded by Steve Turner, has raised $22M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of four same-sector, same-stage private companies (Stark Defence, Castelion, Singularity, and NODA AI) with valuations ranging from $125M to $4.0B, plus two public defense contractors (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression method, using total raised as a proxy for current value, applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A advancement, implying a $44M valuation. The peer-median method anchors to the four-company cohort's median valuation of $700M. The dispersion is material\u2014peer valuations span $125M to $4.0B\u2014reflecting heterogeneity in market position and capital efficiency within the sector.\n\nThe triangulated range spans $37M (floor) to $805M (ceiling), with a median of $372M. This wide band reflects genuine uncertainty: the stage-progression method implies a conservative floor near current capitalization, while peer medians suggest substantially higher value creation potential. Key drivers of uncertainty include Darkhive's competitive positioning relative to peers, revenue trajectory, and customer concentration in an evolving defense procurement environment. A narrower range would require clarity on revenue, unit economics, and customer traction relative to the peer set.",
