      "narrative": "Biofire is a Series A defense & security company founded by Kai Kloepfer that has raised $52.9M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 10 private and public companies in the same sector and stage, including four direct peers: Stark Defence ($4.0B), Castelion ($1.0B), Singularity ($400M), and NODA AI ($125M), alongside public comparables DRSHF and IDEAFORGE.NS.\n\nTwo triangulation methods apply to this stage and sector. The stage-progression method uses total capital raised ($53M) as a proxy base value and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, yielding $106M. The peer-median method references the four same-stage, same-sector peers, which exhibit a median valuation of $700M with a range of $125M to $4.0B, reflecting material heterogeneity in the cohort.\n\nThe triangulated analysis produces a low-to-high range of $90M to $805M, with a median of $403M across both methods. The wide spread reflects the outsized valuations of early-stage defense companies (particularly Stark Defence at $4.0B), which compress the peer distribution significantly. Key uncertainties include the applicability of stage-progression to a capital-intensive defense business and the extent to which Biofire's technology and market position align with the higher-valuation outliers versus the lower-valuation floor in the peer set. Additional diligence on product maturity and customer validation would refine this range.",
