      "narrative": "Albedo is a Series B-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $130M+ to date. The valuation analysis triangulates across a peer set of 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private comparables (Sierra Space at $8.0B Series C, Cowboy Space at $2.0B Series B, Aalyria at $1.3B Series B, and Skyryse at $1.1B Series C), supplemented by stage-progression methodology grounded in the company's cumulative raise.\n\nTwo valuation methods prove applicable. Stage-progression analysis, applying a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement to the $130M raised proxy, implies $247M. Peer-median analysis across the four same-sector comparables yields a median valuation of $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiple is not executable absent disclosed revenue figures.\n\nThe two-method triangulation supports a valuation range of $210M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $948M. The wide dispersion reflects material heterogeneity within the peer set\u2014particularly Sierra Space's $8.0B valuation as an outlier\u2014and uncertainty around Albedo's specific revenue trajectory and competitive position within Space & Aerospace. Stage-progression yields a more conservative view than peer medians, suggesting the range's lower bound warrants consideration given Albedo's Series B status relative to later-stage comparables.",
