      "narrative": "Astrolab, a Series A space and aerospace company founded by Jaret B. Matthews, has raised $40M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 5 public tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, and Planet Labs, with 3 direct same-sector and adjacent-stage private comparables applied to quantitative methods.\n\nTwo triangulation methods proved applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using the $40M total raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, yields $80M. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector comparables\u2014Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B Series B), Aalyria ($1.3B Series B), and Starcloud ($1.1B Seed)\u2014produces a median of $1.3B, with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B. Public-comp anchoring was inapplicable due to the absence of disclosed revenue data for Astrolab. The public sector median P/S multiple of 27.4x across the five tickers cannot be deployed without this input.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $68M (low) to $1.5B (high), with a median of $690M. The wide spread reflects uncertainty around whether Astrolab's technology maturity and commercial traction align with early-stage ($80M) or later-stage peer ($1.3B+) positioning. Revenue disclosure and product validation timelines are material to narrowing this range.",
