      "narrative": "Boston Metal, a Series C climate and energy technology company founded by Sadoway and Allanore, is valued against a universe of 3 same-stage private peers in hard-tech decarbonization (KoBold Metals at $3.0B, Electric Hydrogen at $1.0B, and Amogy at $700M), supplemented by a broader set of 8 private comparables and 1 public reference (Linamar, LNZA).\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using the company's $370M total capital raised as a proxy base, applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement, yielding $629M. Peer-median benchmarking across the three same-sector, same-stage comparables produces a $1.0B implied valuation, with a range spanning $700M to $3.0B. The wide peer dispersion reflects heterogeneous technology maturity and capital efficiency within the climate hardware sector.\n\nTriangulation of both methods produces a valuation range of $535M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $814M. The stage-progression method anchors the lower bound, while peer comparables support the higher end, particularly given KoBold Metals' $3.0B valuation on comparable technical risk. Key uncertainties include technology readiness relative to peers, path to commercialization, and capital efficiency\u2014variables not fully captured in stage-based multiples alone. The $279M spread between low and high estimates reflects material sensitivity to peer selection and method weighting within the emerging decarbonization hardware space.",
