      "narrative": "Atomic Machines is a Series A-stage semiconductor company founded by Jeff Holden that has raised $144M to date. The valuation assessment draws on a comparable universe of 3 same-sector, same-stage private peers (SambaNova Systems at $11.0B, Rebellions at $2.3B, and d-Matrix at $2.0B) and 3 public semiconductor benchmarks (ALAB, NVDA, AMD).\n\nTwo triangulation methods proved applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using total capital raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A advancement, yields $288M. Peer-median benchmarking across the three private comparables produces $2.3B, with the peer range spanning $2.0B to $11.0B. Public-comp anchoring via price-to-sales multiples (sector median 20.5x) was not applicable due to the absence of disclosed revenue figures. \n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $245M (low), $1.3B (median), to $2.7B (high). This wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty: the peer set exhibits substantial heterogeneity in realized valuations, with SambaNova commanding a significant premium. Stage-progression suggests a more conservative baseline, while peer medians anchor toward the higher end. Key unknowns include Atomic Machines' revenue trajectory, competitive positioning within the cohort, and whether Series A capital efficiency aligns with the sample peer group.",
