      "narrative": "Overland AI is a Series A-stage defense and security company that has raised $40M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of four same-sector, same-stage private companies (Stark Defence, Castelion, Singularity, and NODA AI) alongside public market references including DRSHF and IDEAFORGE.NS, supplemented by additional private peers such as Anduril Industries.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression method uses the $40M total raised as a proxy base value and applies a 2.0x multiplier typical for Series A advancement, yielding $80M. The peer-median method derives the median valuation across the four comparable companies at $700M, with a range spanning $125M (NODA AI) to $4.0B (Stark Defence). These disparate results reflect meaningful variance within the defense tech cohort, particularly between companies at the lower end of funding scale versus breakout players.\n\nThe triangulated analysis produces a valuation range of $68M (low) to $805M (high), with a median point of $390M. The substantial spread between methods reflects both the relative infancy of Overland AI's funding stage and the wide dispersion in valuations among peer companies operating in an emerging, capital-intensive sector. Key uncertainties include competitive positioning within the crowded defense AI landscape and revenue traction relative to stage-comparable peers.",
