      "narrative": "Primer AI, a Series D defense and security software company founded by Sean Gourley, has raised $237M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 10 peers\u20142 public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private\u2014within the same sector and stage.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total capital raised as a proxy for current valuation and applying a 1.5x step-up multiplier typical of Series D advancement, implies a valuation of $356M. Peer-median analysis examined four same-stage, same-sector comparables: Helsing ($18.0B), Saronic ($9.2B), Chaos Industries ($4.5B), and Onebrief ($2.1B). The median valuation across this cohort is $6.9B, with a range spanning $2.1B to $18.0B.\n\nThe two methods produce substantially divergent results, reflecting material uncertainty about Primer's positioning within its cohort. The stage-progression approach anchors to capital deployment efficiency, yielding $356M. The peer-median method suggests substantially higher valuations, reflecting defense-tech sector dynamics. Synthesizing both approaches, a triangulated range of $302M (low) to $7.9B (high) is supported, with a median of $3.6B. Key uncertainties include Primer's specific revenue trajectory relative to peers and market appetite for Defense & Security software at varying scales of capital intensity.",
