      "narrative": "Outpost Space is a Seed-stage space and aerospace company founded by Jason Dunn that has raised $40M+. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 5 public peers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private companies in the sector including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, ICEYE, and Sierra Space.\n\nA single applicable triangulation method supports this analysis: stage-progression valuation. Using the $40M total raised as a proxy for current value and applying a typical 2.5x step-up multiplier from Seed to the next financing stage yields an implied valuation of $100M. This multiplier reflects observed dynamics in early-stage aerospace investment where technical risk mitigation and customer validation drive material re-rating between rounds.\n\nThe peer-median and public-comp anchoring methods are not applicable here. The private peer set is too narrow when filtered for same-stage and adjacent-stage comparables (only 1 datapoint at Seed), precluding a robust median. Public comps yield a sector P/S median of 27.4x across the five tickers, but target revenue is not disclosed, making ratio-based valuation impractical. The analysis therefore supports a valuation range of $85M\u2013$115M, centered on $100M. Key uncertainties include the extent of revenue traction at Seed stage and customer concentration, neither addressed in available data.",
