      "narrative": "Medra is a Series A-stage biotech and health company founded by Michelle Lee that has raised $52M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a universe of 3 public comparables (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private peers in the biotech sector, though narrow peer matching proved constrained.\n\nOnly one valuation method proved applicable: Stage-Progression analysis. Using total raised ($52M) as a proxy for Series A value and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to subsequent-stage progression yields an implied valuation of $104M. The Peer-Median approach was not applicable due to insufficient same-stage and adjacent-stage comparables meeting minimum density thresholds (fewer than 3 datapoints across relevant filters). Public-Comp Anchoring could not be applied because Medra's revenue is not on file, preventing meaningful P/S multiple application despite a 9.2x median P/S across the 3 public biotech peers.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $88M (low) to $120M (high), with a median of $104M. This range reflects the single applicable method's output plus standard sensitivity bounds. Key uncertainties include the absence of detailed revenue or operational metrics needed for multiple-based corroboration, the thinness of same-stage private peer data, and the reliance on raised capital as a valuation proxy rather than direct financial performance benchmarking. A narrower, higher-conviction range would require disclosure of revenue, burn rate, or clinical/product milestones.",
