      "narrative": "Heirloom Carbon is a Series B-stage climate and energy company that has raised $150M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 9 private companies and 1 public company (Linamar, LNZA) operating in the Climate & Energy sector, including peers such as KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Amogy.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B-to-next-stage advancement against the $150M total raised proxy, yielding $285M. Peer-median analysis examines three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables: KoBold Metals at $3.0B (Series C), Electric Hydrogen at $1.0B (Series C), and Amogy at $700M (Series C). The median valuation across these three peers is $1.0B, with a range of $700M to $3.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $242M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $642M. Stage-progression implies the lower bound, while peer-median analysis anchors the higher end. Key uncertainties include the appropriate discount for Heirloom's earlier stage relative to Series C comparables and the relevance of public-market comps given sector-specific capital intensity and commercialization risk. The $400M spread between low and high reflects meaningful variance in how frontier-tech development trajectories are valued.",
