      "narrative": "PsiQuantum is a private-stage quantum computing company currently valued at $7.0B, having raised $1.0B to date. The valuation assessment relies on a peer-median approach across six same-sector comparables spanning both public and private quantum computing companies, including Quantinuum ($14.8B, Series G), IonQ ($13.0B, public), D-Wave Quantum ($6.3B, public), SandboxAQ ($5.8B, Series E), and Rigetti Computing ($4.5B, public).\n\nThe peer-median method yields an implied valuation of $6.0B, derived from the median across the six-company universe. The peer set exhibits a wide range from $1.9B to $14.8B, reflecting material variance in stage, technology approach, and commercialization progress within the quantum computing sector. This median of $6.0B sits approximately 14% below PsiQuantum's current $7.0B valuation.\n\nThe triangulated analysis, constrained by the availability of a single applicable method, supports a valuation range of $5.1B to $6.9B (median $6.0B). PsiQuantum's current $7.0B valuation sits modestly above this range. Key uncertainties include heterogeneity in quantum architectures and commercialization timelines across peers, which limits direct comparability. The wide peer dispersion ($1.9B\u2013$14.8B) underscores material uncertainty in quantum computing valuations. Additional methods\u2014revenue multiples or discounted cash flow\u2014would strengthen conviction but lack sufficient data for application here.",
