      "narrative": "Black Semiconductor, a Series A chip design company founded by Daniel and Sebastian Schall, is evaluated against a universe of 8 private peers and 3 public semiconductor comparables (ALAB, NVDA, AMD). The target has raised \u20ac254.4M to date.\n\nTwo valuation methods triangulate to a range. Stage-progression analysis, applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A advancement, yields $509M. Peer-median analysis anchors to three same-sector, same-stage companies (SambaNova Systems at $11.0B, Rebellions at $2.3B, and d-Matrix at $2.0B), producing a median of $2.3B. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (sector median 20.5x) cannot be applied due to lack of revenue disclosure. The wide dispersion among private peers\u2014ranging from $2.0B to $11.0B\u2014reflects uncertainty in the segment.\n\nThe two applicable methods support a triangulated range of $432M (low), $1.4B (median), and $2.7B (high). The median reflects modest weight toward peer multiples given the established comparables, with stage-progression providing a more conservative floor. Key uncertainties include Black Semiconductor's differentiation within a crowded private semiconductor space, the outsized valuation of SambaNova ($11B), and the lack of revenue visibility to calibrate against public multiples.",
