      "narrative": "Exotec, a Series D robotics and manufacturing automation company founded by Romain Moulin and Renaud Heitz, carries a current post-money valuation of $2.0B following $335M+ in total capital raised. The valuation analysis draws from a peer set of nine companies (one public, eight private) operating in robotics and manufacturing automation, including same-stage and adjacent-stage comparables such as Hadrian ($1.6B, Series D), Divergent ($2.3B, Series E), Agile Robots ($1.0B, Series C), and Nimble Robotics ($1.0B, Series C).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, applying a typical 1.5x step-up multiplier from the Series D post-money base, implies a valuation of $3.0B. Peer-median analysis across the four sampled robotics comparables yields a median valuation of $1.3B, with a range spanning $1.0B to $2.3B. The peer set reflects both direct stage comparables and adjacent-stage reference points within the same sector.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a range of $1.1B (low) to $3.4B (high), with a median of $2.1B. The current $2.0B valuation sits near the lower bound of this range, slightly below the methodological median. Key uncertainties center on the appropriate stage-progression multiplier in a shifting capital environment and the relevance of the limited peer sample given Exotec's specific competitive positioning and unit economics relative to comparables.",
