      "narrative": "Neko Health is a Series C-stage biotech & health company founded by Daniel Ek and Hjalmar Nilsonne that has raised $326M+. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 3 public biotech peers (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private frontier-tech companies in the same sector, including Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, and New Limit.\n\nTwo triangulation methods apply. The stage-progression approach uses the $700M total raised as a proxy base value and applies a 1.7x Series C step-up multiplier, implying $1.2B. The peer-median method anchors to 3 same-stage, same-sector private comparables with a median valuation of $3.8B (range: $3.1B\u2013$10.3B). Public-comp anchoring is not applicable due to the absence of disclosed revenue. The resulting triangulated range is $1.0B (low) to $4.4B (high), with a median of $2.5B across both methods.\n\nKey uncertainties include the wide dispersion among private peers, which suggests material differences in technology maturity or go-to-market traction across the peer set, and reliance on stage-progression as a proxy given undisclosed current valuation. The $1.0B\u2013$4.4B range reflects the gap between stage-based extrapolation and peer observation.",
