      "narrative": "ICEYE is a Series F space technology company founded by Rafa\u0142 Modrzewski and Pekka Laurila, currently valued at \u20ac10.5B (~$12.0B) following $650M+ in total raised capital. The valuation assessment relies on a peer universe of 5 Space & Aerospace companies spanning both public equities (Rocket Lab, Planet Labs, Firefly Aerospace) and late-stage private entities (Sierra Space, Impulse Space).\n\nStage-progression methodology was inapplicable; the reported $12.0B post-money valuation implies a multiple exceeding 20x total capital raised, suggesting potential data integrity issues with the baseline figure. Public comparable anchoring was similarly excluded due to absence of disclosed revenue figures, precluding application of the sector median P/S multiple of 27.4x. Consequently, valuation rests on peer-median triangulation: the five comparable companies trade at a median valuation of $7.6B, with a range spanning $2.9B (Firefly Aerospace) to $40.0B (Rocket Lab). This dispersion reflects heterogeneity in maturity and revenue scale across the sector.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $6.4B to $8.7B, centered on the peer median of $7.6B. This implies a modest discount to the company's stated $12.0B valuation. Key uncertainties include revenue scale and growth trajectory relative to public and private comparables, and the extent to which ICEYE's synthetic aperture radar capability and customer base command a premium within the broader aerospace sector.",
