      "narrative": "Saltfoss Energy is a Series A nuclear energy company that has raised $40M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 11 entities across the nuclear sector\u20143 public companies (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 8 private firms including Valar Atomics, Helion, X-Energy, Fuse Energy, and Oklo\u2014spanning seed through Series B stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods apply here. Stage-progression analysis uses the $40M total raised as a proxy base value and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, yielding $80M. Peer-median analysis examines three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables: Valar Atomics at $6.0B (Series B), Nano Nuclear Energy at $808M (Seed), and Fuse Energy at $200M (Series A). The median of these three peers is $808M, with a range spanning $200M to $6.0B. This wide dispersion reflects stage and maturity variation within the nuclear energy sector.\n\nThe triangulated analysis produces a valuation range of $68M to $929M, with a median of $444M. The stage-progression method anchors the lower bound; peer median dominates the upper half. Key uncertainties include technology maturation timelines, regulatory pathway clarity, and capital intensity through commercialization\u2014factors that explain the wide peer range. The $444M median reflects positioning between early-stage peers and more mature Series B competitors.",
