      "narrative": "QuantWare, a Series B quantum computing company founded by Matt Rijlaarsdam and Alessandro Bruno, is evaluated within a fragmented frontier-tech sector comprising 3 public peers (IONQ, RGTI, QBTS) and 8 private competitors including Quantinuum, IonQ, PsiQuantum, D-Wave Quantum, and SandboxAQ.\n\nStage-progression analysis provides the primary valuation anchor. Using QuantWare's $178M in total capital raised as a proxy for current enterprise value, application of a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B advancement yields $338M. This method is the sole quantitative framework applicable given the quantum computing sector's limited comparability across stage and valuation tiers\u2014peer median analysis was not feasible owing to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage datapoints meeting minimum sample thresholds (0 vs. required 3+).\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $287M to $389M, with $338M as the median point. The range reflects stage-progression sensitivity rather than cross-sectional peer calibration. Material uncertainties include the representativeness of the 1.9x multiplier for this particular sector's capital deployment patterns, the stability of the quantum computing competitive set, and achievability of typical Series B-to-C milestone expectations. Given the sparse peer universe and nascent market structure, this valuation carries elevated model risk and should be stress-tested against sector-specific exit multiples and underlying technical progress metrics.",
