      "narrative": "PLD Space is a Series G-stage space and aerospace company that has raised \u20ac120M to date across its funding history. The valuation universe comprises 5 public peers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private comparables including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, ICEYE, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs.\n\nOf three candidate valuation methods, only Stage-Progression proved applicable. Using total raised (\u20ac120M, approximately $209M) as a proxy for enterprise value, a 1.25x step-up multiplier typical for Series G progression yields an implied valuation of $261M. The Peer-Median approach could not be executed: while 14 same-sector private peers exist, the narrow filters (same-stage, adjacent-stage, similar tier) returned fewer than three datapoints, making a reliable median unachievable. Public-Comp Anchoring is inapplicable because PLD Space's revenue is not disclosed; the public universe median P/S multiple of 27.4x cannot be deployed without revenue input.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $222M to $300M, centered on $261M from stage-progression mechanics. This range reflects uncertainty bands around the single applicable method rather than triangulation across multiple approaches. Key uncertainties include the appropriate stage-step multiplier (1.25x assumes mid-market progression), revenue scale relative to peers, and technology readiness relative to public-market comparables. Additional disclosure of revenue or near-term financial metrics would substantially narrow this range.",
