      "narrative": "Ramon.Space is a Series B-stage space & aerospace company that has raised $43.5M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer set of 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private comparables (Sierra Space at $8.0B, Cowboy Space Corporation at $2.0B, Aalyria at $1.3B, and Skyryse at $1.1B), alongside 5 public Space & Aerospace benchmarks (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL).\n\nTwo valuation methods prove applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using total capital raised ($44M proxy) with a typical Series B-to-next-stage step-up multiplier of 1.9x, implies a valuation of $83M. Peer-median analysis across the 4 comparables yields $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied given the absence of disclosed revenue figures, standard for private companies. The public median P/S multiple of 27.4x across the sector remains a directional reference only.\n\nThe triangulation of applicable methods supports a valuation range of $70M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $866M. The substantial spread reflects uncertainty regarding Ramon.Space's specific technology maturity, customer pipeline, and pathway to commercialization relative to peers. Stage-progression yields the tighter, more conservative bound, while peer medians anchor to comparable fundraising and market positioning within an expanding but still-concentrated sector.",
