      "narrative": "ispace is a public-stage Space & Aerospace company founded by Takeshi Hakamada that has raised $200M+. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 4 same-sector, same-stage peers: Rocket Lab ($40.0B), Planet Labs ($7.6B), Firefly Aerospace ($2.9B), and Astroscale ($840M).\n\nThe Peer-Median method is the applicable triangulation approach here. The median valuation across these four public Space & Aerospace comparables is $5.2B, with a range spanning $840M to $40.0B. The Public-Comp Anchoring method using sector P/S multiples (27.4x median across 6 public tickers including RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, and SATL) cannot be applied due to unavailable revenue data for the target company, a common constraint for private-stage businesses.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $4.4B to $6.0B, centered on the peer median of $5.2B. Given the single applicable method and the wide dispersion within the peer set\u2014a 48x spread from floor to ceiling\u2014valuation uncertainty is material. Key drivers of final value within this range include ispace's revenue scale relative to peers, capital efficiency, and market position within lunar logistics and in-space infrastructure segments. The absence of revenue-based anchoring and reliance on a relatively small peer cohort warrant caution in treating this range as precisely calibrated.",
