      "narrative": "Rapidus is a late-stage frontier semiconductor company founded by Atsuyoshi Koike and Tetsuro Higashi. The company has raised $5B+ to date. The Chips & Semiconductors sector includes 3 public comparables (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private peers such as Cerebras, Credo Semiconductor, and SambaNova Systems.\n\nStage-progression analysis is the applicable valuation method here. Using total capital raised of $5.0B as a proxy baseline and applying a 1.2x step-up multiplier typical of late-stage advancement yields an implied valuation of $6.0B. Peer-median triangulation is not supportable due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables within the narrow semiconductor cohort\u2014while 12 same-sector peers exist, none meet the minimum threshold of three datapoints in tightly filtered categories. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples cannot be applied because Rapidus does not disclose revenue, which is standard for private companies at this stage.\n\nThe triangulation supports a valuation range of $5.1B to $6.9B, with a median point of $6.0B. This reflects limited methodological overlap\u2014only one primary method is quantitatively defensible. Key uncertainties include the absence of revenue visibility needed for relative valuation, the scarcity of true peer comparables at identical stage and scale, and reliance on stage-progression mechanics that assume typical funding dynamics. Additional data on operating metrics or capital deployment trajectory would tighten confidence.",
