      "narrative": "Skyroot Aerospace is a Series C-stage space & aerospace company that has raised $160M to date. The valuation analysis employs triangulation across two applicable methods, benchmarked against a comp universe of 6 private peers at Series B\u2013D stages (Sierra Space, Apex Space, Cowboy Space Corporation, Varda Space Industries, and Aalyria) and 5 public-market anchors (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL).\n\nStage-progression methodology applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier to the $160M capital raised proxy, implying a valuation of $272M. Peer-median analysis across the six same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yields $1.8B, with a range of $1.15B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring is not applicable here; while the Space & Aerospace sector trades at a 27.4x median price-to-sales across five public companies, Skyroot's revenue is not disclosed. \n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $231M (low) to $2.1B (high), with a median of $1.0B. The wide dispersion between stage-progression and peer-median results reflects structural differences in capital intensity and exit stage within the aerospace subsector. Key uncertainties include actual revenue generation relative to peer benchmarks, technology differentiation, and execution risk in a capital-intensive, long-cycle business. The peer set spans early-stage ventures to near-IPO entities, limiting precision without revenue normalization.",
