      "narrative": "GrayMatter Robotics is a Series B robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $70M+ to date. Valuation assessment relies on a peer universe of nine private companies and one public comparable (ticker 277810.KQ), including same-stage peers Generalist AI ($2.0B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B), and Dexterity ($1.6B).\n\nTwo methods yield materially different signals. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier to the last post-money valuation of $300M, implying $570M. Peer-median methodology across the three closest same-sector, same-stage comparables yields $1.8B, with a range of $1.6B to $2.0B. The peer set exhibits significant dispersion, suggesting meaningful heterogeneity in investor assessment of robotics businesses at this stage.\n\nTriangulation across both methods supports a valuation range of $484M (low) to $2.0B (high), with a median of $1.2B. The wide spread reflects tension between GrayMatter's earlier-stage funding profile relative to peer valuations. Key uncertainties include: capital efficiency relative to peers, differentiation in technology or market access, and the representativeness of the peer median given limited sample size (n=3). Additional data on revenue, burn rate, or customer concentration would narrow confidence in the range.",
