      "narrative": "Pano AI is a Series B-stage climate and energy company founded by Sonia Kastner and Arvind Satyam that has raised $89M to date. Valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 9 private companies and 1 public company (Linamar, ticker LNZA) in the Climate & Energy sector, including peer-stage assessments of KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Amogy.\n\nTwo valuation methods triangulate to a midpoint of $975M. The stage-progression method applies a 1.9x multiplier to the last known post-money valuation of $500M, implying $950M. The peer-median method identifies three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables with a median valuation of $1.0B and a range of $700M to $3.0B, implying $1.0B. These methods converge closely, with a low bound of $808M and high bound of $1.1B.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $808M to $1.1B, centered at $975M. Key uncertainties include the wide dispersion in the peer set (a 4.3x spread between floor and ceiling), the limited visibility into Pano AI's specific unit economics relative to the peer cohort, and the nascent commercialization status typical of Series B climate-tech companies. The peer-median method carries somewhat higher conviction given the sample size and sector alignment.",
