      "narrative": "Orangewood Labs is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $5M+ to date. The valuation analysis triangulates across a comp universe of 9 private firms and 1 public company in the robotics sector, including peers such as Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, Generalist AI, and Walden Robotics at Series B and Seed stages.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $10M total-raised proxy as a base and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, implying a $20M valuation. Peer-median analysis draws from four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables with a median valuation of $1.7B and a range of $1.1B to $2.0B. The peer set skews toward more mature Series B financings, which structurally inflates the median relative to Orangewood's current stage.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a wide range: $17M (low), $860M (median), and $2.0B (high). The disparity reflects material uncertainty in stage mapping and growth trajectory. The stage-progression method yields a conservative floor anchored to capital deployed; the peer-median is heavily influenced by later-stage Series B valuations that may not be directly comparable to an early Series A position. Key uncertainties include revenue traction, capital efficiency, and competitive positioning within manufacturing automation\u2014factors not captured in the data provided and essential to narrowing this range.",
