      "narrative": "Starpath Robotics is a Series A-stage Space & Aerospace company founded by Saurav Shroff, Mihir Gondhalekar, and Jason Zang. The company has raised $14.5M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 5 public Space & Aerospace equities (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers spanning the sector.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 2.0x multiplier to a $50M base derived from total capital raised, implying a $100M valuation consistent with typical Series A step-ups. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables (Cowboy Space at $2.0B Series B, Aalyria at $1.3B Series B, and Starcloud at $1.1B Seed) yields a $1.3B median with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B. Public-comp anchoring using the Space & Aerospace sector P/S median of 27.4x cannot be applied, as target revenue is not disclosed.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range spans $85M (low) to $1.5B (high), with a median of $700M. The wide dispersion reflects tension between bottom-up stage progression logic and the outsized valuations commanded by late-stage peers in an infrastructure-heavy sector with high capital intensity and significant technical risk. Key uncertainties include revenue trajectory, customer traction, and technical validation milestones that would narrow this range materially.",
