      "narrative": "LeoLabs is a Series B space and aerospace company that has raised $94M to date. The valuation analysis relies on a peer set of four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private companies (Sierra Space at $8.0B, Cowboy Space Corporation at $2.0B, Aalyria at $1.3B, and Skyryse at $1.1B), supplemented by five publicly traded Space & Aerospace comps trading at a median 27.4x price-to-sales.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a typical 1.9x step-up multiplier to the $94M total raised proxy, implying a $179M valuation. Peer-median analysis across the four private comparables yields a $1.6B implied value, with the range spanning $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied due to absence of revenue disclosure for the target.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $152M to $1.9B, with a median of $914M across the two applicable methods. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty: the peer set exhibits substantial heterogeneity (8.0x spread from min to max), and stage-progression relies on a simplified multiplier approach that may not capture LeoLabs' specific market position or unit economics. Resolution of this range will require clarity on LeoLabs' current revenue trajectory, customer concentration, and technical differentiation relative to the peer cohort.",
