      "narrative": "Locus Robotics, a Series F robotics and manufacturing company, was last valued at $2.0B post-money after raising $438M cumulatively. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 9 same-sector comparables at similar valuation tiers, comprising 8 private companies and 1 public entity. Key private peers include Divergent ($2.3B, Series E), Exotec ($2.0B, Series D), and Dexterity ($1.6B, Series B), with the peer set ranging from $1.0B to $2.3B.\n\nTwo methods were applied. Stage-progression modeling, using a typical 1.3x step-up multiplier from Series F to the next stage, implies a valuation of $2.6B. Peer-median analysis across the 9-company cohort yields $1.6B, reflecting the dispersion introduced by earlier-stage peers carrying similar valuations. The peer median sits below the current post-money valuation, suggesting Locus's current terms price ahead of stage-matched medians.\n\nTriangulation across both methods produces a range of $1.4B to $3.0B, with a median of $2.1B. The current $2.0B valuation falls within this range, near the lower end of the triangulated band. Key uncertainties include the heterogeneity of peer stages within the comparable set and the limited public-market reference point, which constrains calibration of exit-multiple expectations.",
