      "narrative": "Lumafield is a Series C robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $142M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 9 private robotics firms at Series B\u2013D stages, including Exotec ($2.0B Series D), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B Series B), and Hadrian ($1.6B Series D), alongside one public comparable.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression method, anchoring to the $10M total-raised proxy and applying a 1.7x Series C step-up multiplier, yields $17M. The peer-median method uses the median valuation across 7 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables, which stands at $1.6B, with a range of $1.0B to $2.0B. These methods produce substantially divergent signals, reflecting the wide dispersion in robotics valuations at this maturity band.\n\nThe triangulated midpoint across both methods is $834M, with a low bound of $14M and a high bound of $1.9B. The wide range reflects genuine uncertainty: the stage-progression method implies significantly lower value, while the peer-median approach anchors to recent market pricing for robotics firms at overlapping stages. Key uncertainties include revenue scale relative to peers, unit economics, and the degree to which Lumafield's technology or market position merits a premium or discount to the median comp valuation.",
