      "narrative": "Nord Quantique is a Seed-stage quantum computing company founded by Julien Camirand Lemyre and Philippe St-Jean. The company has raised C$40M+ to date, including C$23M from the Quantum Champions fund in December 2025. The quantum computing sector comprises 3 public peers and 8 private competitors including Quantinuum, IonQ, PsiQuantum, D-Wave Quantum, and SandboxAQ.\n\nValuation analysis relies on the Stage-Progression method, as peer-median analysis is not applicable. The Seed-to-next-stage cohort typically commands a 2.5x multiplier; applied to the C$40M+ total raised as a proxy for current base value, this yields an implied valuation of $100M. This method captures the expected step-function increase in value between financing rounds typical of frontier-technology companies at this stage.\n\nThe analysis supports a triangulated range of $85M to $115M, with a median point of $100M. This range reflects the single applicable methodology and should be considered subject to material uncertainty. Key risks include the absence of narrowly comparable Seed-stage peers in quantum computing\u2014a sector where financing patterns, technical milestones, and path-to-revenue remain highly heterogeneous. The valuation is sensitive to the assumptions embedded in stage-progression multipliers and would benefit from crystallized commercial or technical inflection points before the next financing round.",
