      "narrative": "Kepler Communications is a Series C-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $200M+ to date. The valuation analysis triangulates across two applicable methods, benchmarking against a comp set of 6 same-sector peers at Series B\u2013D stages, including Sierra Space ($8.0B), Apex Space ($2.3B), Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B), Varda Space Industries ($1.6B), and Aalyria ($1.3B).\n\nStage-progression analysis applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier to the $200M raised proxy, implying a $340M valuation. Peer-median valuation across the 6 comparable companies yields $1.8B, with a range of $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring is not applicable because Kepler's revenue is not disclosed, precluding use of the Space & Aerospace sector median P/S multiple of 27.4x across five public tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL).\n\nThe two applicable methods produce a triangulated range of $289M (low) to $2.1B (high), with a median of $1.1B. The wide dispersion reflects significant uncertainty in peer valuations\u2014particularly Sierra Space's outlier $8.0B valuation\u2014and the absence of revenue-based cross-checks. Key sensitivities include Kepler's revenue trajectory, customer concentration, and how comparable its business model is to the heterogeneous peer set spanning launch, in-space manufacturing, and satellite communications.",
