      "narrative": "Reaction Dynamics is a Series A-stage space and aerospace company founded by Bachar Elzein that has raised C$38M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers spanning similar and adjacent stages, including Rocket Lab, ICEYE, and Sierra Space.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier from the $38M capital raised proxy, implying a $76M valuation. Peer-median anchoring draws on three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private comparables\u2014Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B, Series B), Aalyria ($1.3B, Series B), and Starcloud ($1.1B, Seed)\u2014yielding a median valuation of $1.3B with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B. Public comparable anchoring cannot be applied, as target revenue is not on file. The public sector median trading multiple is 27.4x across 6 tickers, but without Reaction Dynamics' revenue disclosure, this method remains inaccessible.\n\nThe two applicable methods produce a wide triangulated range of $65M (low) to $1.5B (high), with a median of $688M. This substantial dispersion reflects the tension between early-stage capital-raised metrics and later-stage peer valuations. Key uncertainties center on whether comparables reflect comparable technology maturity, go-to-market stage, and capital efficiency. Revenue visibility and customer traction would narrow this range materially.",
