      "narrative": "Swift Beat, a Series A-stage Defense & Security company founded by Eric Schmidt, has raised $50M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 10 peers: 2 public companies (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms including Stark Defence, Castelion, Singularity, NODA AI, and Anduril Industries.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using the $50M total raised as a valuation proxy and applying a typical 2.0x Series A step-up multiplier, implies a valuation of $100M. Peer-median analysis across four same-sector, same-stage private comparables\u2014Stark Defence ($4.0B), Castelion ($1.0B), Singularity ($400M), and NODA AI ($125M)\u2014yields a median valuation of $700M, with a range spanning $125M to $4.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $85M to $805M, with a median of $400M. This wide range reflects substantial dispersion within the peer set, driven primarily by the outsized valuations of Stark Defence and Castelion relative to the floor established by NODA AI. Key uncertainties include Swift Beat's revenue trajectory, customer traction within the Defense & Security sector, and whether the company's competitive positioning aligns with high-end or lower-quartile comparable valuations. Additional clarity on product-market fit and contract wins would narrow this band materially.",
