      "narrative": "Hidden Level, a Series C defense and security company founded by Jeff Cole and Gary Dominicos, has raised $130M to date. The valuation analysis draws on two primary methods triangulated against a peer set of 12 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage companies, comprising 2 public comparables (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private peers including Quantum-Systems, Helsing, Saronic, and Anduril Industries, with valuations ranging from $300M to $18.0B.\n\nStage-progression methodology applies a 1.7x multiplier to the $130M total raised proxy, implying a valuation of $221M. Peer-median analysis across the 12-company Defense & Security cohort yields a median valuation of $2.3B. The disparity between methods reflects meaningful variation within the peer set: while adjacent-stage peers like Dream Security (Series B, $3.0B) and Quantum-Systems (Series C, $8.0B) anchor the upper range, earlier comparables weighted downward. No revenue or margin data were supplied to support cash-flow or profitability-based approaches.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $188M (low) to $2.7B (high), with a median of $1.3B. This wide spread reflects uncertainty around Hidden Level's relative competitive position within a heterogeneous peer cohort and the absence of operational performance metrics. Revenue scale, customer concentration, and technology differentiation versus named peers represent critical validation points for narrowing the range.",
