      "narrative": "Quantinuum, a Series G quantum computing company that has raised $2.7B+ to date, is valued at $14.77B post-money. The quantum computing sector comp universe includes 5 same-sector peers spanning both public equities (IonQ at $13.0B, D-Wave Quantum at $6.3B, Rigetti Computing at $4.5B) and private rounds (PsiQuantum at $7.0B, SandboxAQ at $5.8B), providing reasonable anchors across development stages.\n\nTwo valuation methods triangulate meaningfully. The stage-progression method, applying a 1.25x multiplier typical of Series G step-ups to the $14.8B last post-money valuation, implies $18.5B. The peer-median method across the five-company comp set yields $6.3B, with a range from $4.5B to $13.0B. The wide dispersion reflects genuine heterogeneity in quantum computing architectures, commercialization timelines, and investor conviction across the cohort.\n\nSynthesizing these two approaches yields a triangulated range of $5.3B (low), $12.4B (median), and $21.2B (high). The current $14.77B valuation sits above the median but well below the high case, suggesting the market is pricing Quantinuum at a meaningful premium to peers on the median basis, likely reflecting either superior technical execution or stage-of-development advantages relative to the comp set. Key uncertainties include quantum utility timelines, sustained funding availability in the sector, and the degree to which Quantinuum's specific qubit technology and software stack command differentiated economics versus listed competitors.",
