      "narrative": "OpenStar, a seed-stage nuclear energy company founded by Ratu Mataira and Thomas Berry, has raised $35M to date. The nuclear energy sector comp universe includes 3 public peers (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 8 private companies, among them Nano Nuclear Energy, Helion, Oklo, Valar Atomics, and X-Energy. However, the narrow peer set for seed-stage nuclear ventures proved insufficient for reliable median-multiple triangulation\u2014only 1 same-stage comparable and 1 adjacent-stage peer were identified, falling short of the minimum 3 datapoints required for statistical confidence.\n\nThe Stage-Progression method was therefore the applicable approach. Using OpenStar's $35M total raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.5x multiplier typical of seed-to-next-stage progression, the analysis implies a valuation of $87.5M. This single-method result anchors the range.\n\nGiven the limited methodological diversity, the triangulated valuation range is $74M (low), $88M (median), and $101M (high), with the median reflecting the stage-progression result. The range reflects reasonable sensitivity around the single-method point estimate but should be regarded with caution. Key uncertainties include the appropriateness of the 2.5x step-up multiplier for the specific subsector and competitive positioning of OpenStar relative to the broader nuclear energy landscape. Additional private comparable data or revenue-based approaches would strengthen conviction in this range.",
