      "narrative": "MacroFab is a Series C robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $141M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of nine peers\u2014one public company (277810.KQ) and eight private firms spanning Series B through Series D, including Exotec, Dexterity, Hadrian, Bedrock Robotics, and Locus Robotics.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement to the $141M total raised proxy, yielding $240M. Peer-median analysis across seven same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yields a median valuation of $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.0B to $2.0B. The peer sample includes Exotec at $2.0B (Series D), Hadrian at $1.6B (Series D), Dexterity at $1.6B (Series B), and Bedrock Robotics at $1.8B (Series B).\n\nTriangulation of both methods implies a valuation range of $204M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $945M. The wide dispersion reflects meaningful stage and maturity variance within the peer set and uncertainty regarding MacroFab's relative progress on unit economics, customer concentration, and technology differentiation. Stage-progression yields the conservative bound; peer valuation anchors the upper bound. A defensible range would narrow around $600M\u2013$1.2B pending clarity on revenue trajectory and gross margins relative to the peer cohort.",
