      "narrative": "Finwave Semiconductor is a Series A chip design company founded by Tomas Palacios and Bin Lu, evaluated against a universe of 3 public semiconductor comps (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private peers, with focus on 3 direct-stage comparables: SambaNova Systems ($11.0B), Rebellions ($2.3B), and d-Matrix ($2.0B).\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis uses the company's $25M total raised as a proxy base value and applies a 2.0x multiplier typical of Series A advancement, implying $50M. Peer-median analysis across the three same-sector, same-stage comparables yields a $2.3B median valuation, with a range spanning $2.0B to $11.0B. Public-comp anchoring via price-to-sales (median 20.5x across the three public tickers) cannot be applied absent disclosed revenue figures.\n\nThe two applicable methods produce a wide triangulated range: $42.5M at the low end, $1.2B at the median, and $2.7B at the high end. This dispersion reflects material uncertainty inherent to early-stage frontier semiconductors. Stage-progression conservatively anchors the lower bound, while peer-median dominates the central estimate given the specificity of same-stage comparables. Key uncertainties include whether Finwave's technology trajectory and capital efficiency will track toward the $2.0\u2013$2.3B band (Rebellions, d-Matrix) or command outlier valuation like SambaNova. Revenue generation timeline and competitive positioning within the chip-design subsector remain critical determinants.",
