      "narrative": "RISE Robotics is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Arron Acosta and Blake Sessions that has raised $22M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of 9 private companies and 1 public comparable in the Robotics & Manufacturing sector.\n\nTwo triangulation methods apply here. Stage-progression analysis uses total raised as a proxy base ($22M) and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A advancement, implying a $44M valuation. Peer-median analysis examines four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Generalist AI ($2.0B, Series B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B, Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B, Series B), and Walden Robotics ($1.1B, Seed)\u2014yielding a median valuation of $1.7B with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B.\n\nThe two methods produce materially divergent results, with stage-progression implying $44M and peer-median implying $1.7B. A triangulated range of $37M to $2.0B (median $872M) reflects this spread. The wide dispersion highlights substantive uncertainty: stage-progression may underweight the company's operational traction relative to deployed capital, while peer-median may not adequately discount for stage differential between Series A and the predominantly Series B peer set. Resolution requires clarity on RISE's revenue, unit economics, customer concentration, and technology defensibility relative to the peer universe.",
