      "narrative": "Corvex Systems is a seed-stage robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $5M+. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of nine private robotics firms and one public comparable (ticker 277810.KQ), including peers such as Walden Robotics, Divergent, Exotec, Locus Robotics, and Generalist AI.\n\nThe stage-progression method is the primary applicable approach, using the $5M raised as a proxy for current valuation and applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of seed-to-next-stage advancement. This yields an implied valuation of $12.5M. A peer-median approach could not be applied due to insufficient narrow peer comparables; while the robotics sector contains ten same-sector peers, the dataset lacks three or more datapoints at identical or adjacent stages with comparable valuation tiers, making sector-wide medians unreliable.\n\nThe triangulated analysis, supported by the single applicable method, places Corvex in a $11M\u2013$14M range with a median of $12M. This narrow range reflects methodological constraints rather than convergence across multiple approaches. Key uncertainties include the strength of founder execution (Jason Blick's background and prior outcomes), progress toward product-market fit, and the composition of the $5M+ raise across tranches, which could materially shift the appropriate base valuation. The absence of robust peer-stage comparables limits confidence in the step-up multiplier's applicability to this specific company.",
