      "narrative": "Foundry Lab is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company led by David Moodie that has raised $15M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of nine comparable companies\u2014one public and eight private\u2014spanning robotics and manufacturing at similar or adjacent stages, including Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, Generalist AI, and Walden Robotics.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $15M total raised as a proxy base value and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, yielding $30M. Peer-median analysis references four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables with a median valuation of $1.7B and a range of $1.1B to $2.0B (Walden Robotics at the low end, Generalist AI at $2.0B).\n\nThe wide dispersion between methods\u2014$30M from stage-progression versus $1.7B from peer-median\u2014reflects fundamental uncertainty. The peer set exhibits material heterogeneity in stage advancement and maturity; three comparables are Series B while one is Seed-stage. A reasonable valuation range emerges between $26M and $2.0B, with a triangulated median of $865M. The key uncertainties are the appropriateness of the peer median given Foundry Lab's earlier stage relative to most comparables, and whether raised capital genuinely anchors Series A valuation or merely sets a floor.",
