      "narrative": "Voyant Photonics is a Series A semiconductor company founded by Chris Phare and Steven Miller that has raised $23M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 3 public semiconductor firms (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private peers, with direct stage-and-sector comparables including SambaNova Systems ($11.0B), Rebellions ($2.3B), and d-Matrix ($2.0B).\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression anchors to the $23M raised as a proxy for current value and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A-to-next-stage progression, implying $46M. Peer-median valuation uses the 3 same-stage, same-sector private comparables, yielding a median of $2.3B with a range of $2.0B to $11.0B. Public-comp anchoring (P/S at 20.5x median across the three public tickers) is not applicable due to lack of revenue disclosure. \n\nThe triangulated range spans $39M (low) to $2.7B (high), with a median of $1.2B. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around Voyant's relative competitive positioning within the cohort. The peer-median method dominates the range, though the stage-progression floor suggests downside protection at approximately $46M. Key uncertainties center on differentiation relative to better-capitalized peers like SambaNova and traction metrics not visible in public data.",
