      "narrative": "First Resonance is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $40.8M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of nine peers across robotics and manufacturing\u2014one public company (277810.KQ) and eight private firms including Divergent, Exotec, Locus Robotics, Generalist AI, and Bedrock Robotics, among others.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $41M total raised as a proxy base and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, yielding $82M. Peer-median analysis examines four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables: Generalist AI ($2.0B, Series B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B, Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B, Series B), and Walden Robotics ($1.1B, Seed). This peer set generates a median valuation of $1.7B, with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B.\n\nThe two methods produce a wide implied range: $69M on the low end (stage-progression methodology), $891M at the median, and $2.0B on the high end (peer median). Key uncertainties driving this dispersion include the stage mismatch between First Resonance (Series A) and most comparable peers (predominantly Series B), unit economics and revenue traction not visible in this dataset, and market sentiment in robotics funding. A credible valuation would require reconciliation of these outliers through deeper diligence on growth trajectory and competitive positioning.",
