      "narrative": "Cascade Space is a seed-stage space and aerospace company founded by Jacob Portukalian and Arlen Abraham, having raised $5.9M to date. The valuation exercise draws from a sector universe of 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, and ICEYE.\n\nStage-progression analysis provides the primary valuation signal. Using total capital raised ($6M) as a proxy for seed-stage valuation and applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier\u2014standard for progression from seed to next stage\u2014yields an implied valuation of $15M. Peer-median triangulation was not applicable due to insufficient same- or adjacent-stage comparables in the narrow space and aerospace segment (only 1 same-stage peer identified). Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (median 27.4x across the five public tickers) could not be applied absent revenue disclosure, typical for early-stage private companies.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $13M to $17M, with a median point of $15M. This range reflects \u00b115% sensitivity around the stage-progression calculation. Key uncertainties include the limited applicability of peer benchmarking data at the seed stage and the absence of revenue metrics to cross-check valuation via public multiples. The single-method conclusion warrants updating as the company approaches next-stage fundraising, when comparable transaction data should become more readily available.",
