      "narrative": "Lunar Energy is a Series D climate and energy company founded by Kunal Girotra that has raised over $300M to date. The valuation assessment draws on a peer universe of 9 comparable companies\u20141 public (LNZA) and 8 private entities operating in climate and energy across similar or adjacent funding stages. Primary comparables include Redwood Materials, KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Amogy, spanning valuations from $700M to $6.0B.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. The stage-progression method applies a 1.5x multiplier to the $300M raised proxy, implying a $450M valuation. The peer-median method references four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage companies with a median valuation of $2.0B and a range of $700M to $6.0B, implying $2.0B for Lunar Energy. Reconciling these approaches yields a triangulated valuation range of $382M (low) to $2.3B (high), with a median of $1.2B.\n\nThe dispersion reflects meaningful uncertainty around Lunar Energy's relative position within the peer cohort. The wide peer range\u2014anchored by Amogy at $700M and Redwood Materials at $6.0B\u2014suggests that technology maturity, capital intensity, and commercialization progress drive substantial valuation variance. Without visibility into Lunar's specific operational metrics and path to revenue relative to these comps, the $1.2B median should be treated as a central estimate subject to upside or downside revision based on business fundamentals.",
