      "narrative": "Cache Energy, a Seed-stage climate and energy company founded by Arpit Dwivedi, has raised $8.5M to date. The sector comprises 9 comparable companies\u20141 public (Lonza Group, ticker LNZA) and 8 private peers including Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Enovix\u2014though narrow peer comparability at the Seed stage remains constrained.\n\nValuation analysis relies on stage-progression methodology, the sole applicable triangulation approach given insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage peers meeting statistical thresholds. Using total capital raised ($8.5M) as a base proxy and applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage advancement yields an implied valuation of $21M. The peer-median method was inapplicable; while 8 same-sector companies exist, none satisfied filtering criteria (same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar-valuation-tier) necessary to derive a meaningful comparable dataset.\n\nThe analysis supports a range of $18M to $24M, with a median estimate of $21M. This reflects a conservative 15% discount and 15% premium around the stage-progression result. Key uncertainties include the representativeness of the 2.5x multiplier for this particular subsector and the absence of direct peer valuation anchors, which limits confidence in the range. Additional data on recent Seed financings in advanced energy or materials technology would strengthen conviction.",
