      "narrative": "Verdant Robotics, founded by Gabe Sibley and Curtis Garner, is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $58M to date. The valuation analysis triangulates against a peer set of four same-sector, same- or adjacent-stage private companies\u2014Generalist AI ($2.0B Series B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B Series B), and Walden Robotics ($1.1B Seed)\u2014supplemented by a broader comparison universe of eight private peers and one public comparable.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using a 2.0x step-up multiplier from the $58M total raised proxy, implies a valuation of $116M. Peer-median analysis, computed across the four-company sample, yields a median valuation of $1.7B, with observed range of $1.1B to $2.0B. The wide disparity reflects stage and maturity variation within the peer set: two comparables are Series B, one is Seed, introducing both upside and downside anchor points.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $99M (low) to $2.0B (high), with a median of $908M. Key uncertainty centers on the appropriate stage-discount relative to Series B peers; Verdant's Series A status versus the predominantly Series B composition of the peer median creates material ambiguity. Capital efficiency and revenue/unit economics versus peers would be required to narrow this band meaningfully.",
