      "narrative": "NextSilicon, a Series B chip design company founded by Elad Raz, is valued against a frontier semiconductor landscape. The applicable comp universe spans 8 private and 3 public semiconductor firms, including stage-adjacent peers such as Positron AI (Series B, $1.0B), SambaNova Systems (Series A, $11.0B), and public anchors NVDA, AMD, and ALAB. NextSilicon has raised $200M+ to date.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis, anchoring to the $200M raised proxy and applying a 1.9x Series B step-up multiplier, yields $380M. Peer-median methodology across five same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014median valuation $2.0B, range $529M to $11.0B\u2014supports a $2.0B midpoint. Public comp anchoring cannot be applied: the public semiconductor median P/S of 20.5x is calculable across ALAB, NVDA, and AMD, but NextSilicon's revenue is not disclosed. \n\nThe two applicable methods bracket a valuation range of $323M (low) to $2.3B (high), with a median of $1.2B. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around relative product maturity, IP defensibility, and market timing within the chip subsector. Stage-progression is conservative; peer-median is anchored by a handful of outlier-valued Series A rounds. Near-term disclosure of revenue, unit economics, and design win pipeline would narrow this range materially.",
