      "narrative": "Ideon Technologies is a Series B-stage climate and energy company founded by Gary Agnew that has raised $30M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of nine private firms and one public company (Liontown Resources, LNZA) operating in the same sector, including late-stage peers such as KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Amogy.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression method, using total capital raised as a proxy for valuation and applying a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B advancement, implied a valuation of $57M. The peer-median method examined three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables with valuations spanning $700M to $3.0B; the median valuation across this cohort was $1.0B. Given the disparity between these two signals, a weighted triangulation across both methods yielded a low estimate of $48M, a median of $528M, and a high of $1.1B.\n\nThe wide range reflects material uncertainty around stage-appropriate valuation for frontier climate tech. The stage-progression method anchors conservatively to realized capital; the peer-median approach reflects valuations of more mature Series C entities. Resolution hinges on technology differentiation, path to commercialization, and capital efficiency relative to named comparables. A valuation in the $80M\u2013$250M range may better reflect typical Series B positioning within this cohort.",
