      "narrative": "Enovix is a publicly traded Climate & Energy company currently valued at $1.0B, having raised $700M+ to date. The valuation exercise draws from a peer set of three same-sector, same-stage public comparables: QuantumScape ($3.6B), Solid Power ($504M), and LanzaTech ($73M), with an additional eight private peers tracked for context.\n\nThe peer-median method serves as the primary triangulation approach, yielding a median valuation of $504M across the three public comparables. This method captures meaningful dispersion in the peer universe\u2014a 50x spread between the low ($73M) and high ($3.6B)\u2014reflecting heterogeneity in execution, commercialization timelines, and investor sentiment within the battery and energy storage subsector. The median represents a 1.98x haircut to Enovix's current $1.0B valuation.\n\nAnalysis supports a range of $428M to $580M, centered on $504M. The current $1.0B valuation implies a premium of approximately 98% relative to peer-median, a gap that would require either superior commercialization progress, margin or scale assumptions, or subsector-specific risk repricing not evident in the available data. Key uncertainties include the explanatory power of a three-company peer set, the comparability of private peers (Redwood Materials, KoBold Metals) to public market pricing, and whether Enovix's technology or market position justifies median departure.",
