      "narrative": "Aclarity is a Series A climate and energy technology company founded by Julie Bliss Mullen that has raised $14M to date. The relevant comp universe comprises one public company (LNZA) and eight private peers in the Climate & Energy sector, including Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Enovix. However, no peers share Aclarity's exact stage and valuation tier, limiting peer-median applicability.\n\nWith insufficient same-stage and adjacent-stage comparables (fewer than three datapoints in narrow filters), the Stage-Progression method provides the primary valuation anchor. This approach applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A-to-next-stage progression to the $14M total raised proxy, yielding $28M. A sensitivity range around this single method\u2014accounting for typical variance in step-up multiples\u2014supports a valuation corridor of $24M to $32M.\n\nThe median implied valuation is $28M. Key uncertainties center on the appropriate step-up multiple for this specific sector (climate tech exhibits heterogeneous growth trajectories) and the company's relative positioning within the broad Climate & Energy landscape. Obtaining comparable transaction data or closer peer financials would strengthen conviction. This range should be stress-tested against management guidance, unit economics, and pathway to Series B.",
