      "narrative": "Akash Systems is a Series B space and aerospace company that has raised $40M+ to date. The valuation analysis triangulates across a peer set of 4 private comparables in the same sector and stage (Sierra Space at $8.0B, Cowboy Space Corporation at $2.0B, Aalyria at $1.3B, and Skyryse at $1.1B), supplemented by 5 public Space & Aerospace comps trading at a median 27.4x price-to-sales.\n\nTwo methods proved applicable. The stage-progression approach uses the company's $40M raised as a proxy for current valuation and applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B advancement, implying $76M. The peer-median method directly references the 4-company comparable universe, yielding a $1.6B implied valuation with a range of $1.1B to $8.0B. Public comps anchoring was not applicable given the absence of revenue data. Triangulating these two methods produces a low estimate of $65M, a median of $863M, and a high of $1.9B.\n\nThe wide dispersion between methods reflects genuine uncertainty in early-stage space tech valuations. The peer set exhibits substantial heterogeneity\u2014ranging from $1.1B to $8.0B\u2014suggesting either material differences in technology, market traction, or funding dynamics across portfolio companies. The stage-progression method likely understates value given the company's post-Series B trajectory, while the peer median may overstate if Akash lacks comparable scale or unit economics. A valuation in the $400M\u2013$1.2B range appears defensible pending disclosure of revenue or ARR metrics and strategic milestones.",
