      "narrative": "Strider Technologies is a Series C-stage defense and security company that has raised $117M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of 12 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage companies, including 2 public comparables (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private peers such as Quantum-Systems ($8.0B, Series C), Helsing ($18.0B, Series D), and Saronic ($9.2B, Series D). The peer universe spans $300M to $18.0B in valuation.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement to the $117M total capital raised proxy, implying a valuation of $199M. Peer-median analysis across the 12-company defense and security cohort yields a median valuation of $2.3B, with a range of $300M to $18.0B. The stark divergence reflects wide dispersion in stage maturity and operational scale within the peer set.\n\nSynthesizing both methods produces a triangulated range of $169M (low) to $2.7B (high), with a median point of $1.3B. The wide band reflects material uncertainty around Strider's relative market position and revenue traction versus peers. Near-term clarity on revenue growth rates, customer concentration, and competitive positioning will be critical to narrowing this range. Stage-progression alone appears to underweight the company relative to established sector peers.",
