      "narrative": "Mythic is a Series D-stage chip design company that has raised $125M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a universe of 8 private semiconductor peers at similar or adjacent funding stages, plus 3 public semiconductor comparables (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) held as sector anchors.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.5x step-up multiplier typical of Series D advancement, yielding $188M. Peer-median analysis examines four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage companies: Etched ($5.0B, Series E), Ayar Labs ($3.8B, Series E), Tenstorrent ($2.7B, Series D), and DEEPX ($529M, Series C). This cohort produces a median valuation of $3.2B with a range of $529M to $5.0B. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (median 20.5x across the sector) is not applicable absent disclosed revenue figures, standard for private companies.\n\nThe triangulated range is $159M (low), $1.7B (median), and $3.7B (high). Stage-progression yields the floor; peer median anchors the midpoint. The wide dispersion\u2014driven by heterogeneous stage mix and capital efficiency across the peer set\u2014reflects material uncertainty around Mythic's technology differentiation, go-to-market readiness, and market timing relative to comparables. Further narrowing requires clarity on revenue traction, design wins, and manufacturing partnerships.",
