      "narrative": "Signaloid is a Seed-stage semiconductor company that has raised $10M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 8 private peers in the Chips & Semiconductors sector at similar or adjacent stages, including SambaNova Systems, Rebellions, and d-Matrix, alongside 3 public semiconductor benchmarks (ALAB, NVDA, AMD).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-Progression applies a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical for Seed-to-next-stage advancement, implying a valuation of $25M. Peer-Median anchors to the median valuation of three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables: SambaNova Systems ($11.0B), Rebellions ($2.3B), and d-Matrix ($2.0B), yielding a median of $2.3B with a range of $2.0B to $11.0B. Public-Comp Anchoring via P/S multiples is not applicable due to lack of disclosed revenue data. The wide dispersion across peer valuations reflects heterogeneous capital intensity and development stage within the semiconductor sector.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a range of $21M (low) to $2.7B (high), with a median of $1.2B. Given Signaloid's Seed stage relative to Series A peers, the low end appears more defensible. Key uncertainties include the company's technology differentiation, IP moat, and path to revenue generation relative to higher-valued peers, as well as the extent of selection bias in the peer set.",
