      "narrative": "Apis Cor is a seed-stage construction technology company that has raised $5.5M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer set of five private companies in the housing and construction technology sector, including BotBuilt, Unlimited Industries, Ground Control Development, ADMARES, and Hedral. No public comparables exist in this niche market segment.\n\nThe stage-progression method is applicable here and forms the basis of the triangulation. Using total capital raised ($5.5M) as a proxy for seed-stage valuation, a standard 2.5x multiplier for progression to Series A yields an implied valuation of $13.75M. This reflects typical dilution and value creation expected between seed and next-round funding in construction tech. The method assumes market conditions and company trajectory align with historical step-ups in the sector.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $12M to $16M, with a median of $14M. This relatively tight band reflects reliance on a single methodological input. Key uncertainties include the representativeness of the five-company peer set\u2014particularly whether those firms' stage-progression dynamics match Apis Cor's market position, burn rate, and go-to-market trajectory. Additional leverage from revenue traction, product differentiation, or team composition would narrow this range but cannot be quantified from available data. The analysis is most robust as a baseline for negotiations rather than a definitive valuation.",
