      "narrative": "SiPearl is a Series A semiconductor chip company founded by Philippe Notton that has raised \u20ac130M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer set of 8 private and 3 public comparables in the Chips & Semiconductors sector, including SambaNova Systems, Rebellions, d-Matrix, Cerebras, and Credo Semiconductor among private firms, and ALAB, NVDA, and AMD as public anchors.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis uses the \u20ac130M raised as a valuation proxy and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A progression, implying a $260M valuation. Peer-median analysis across three same-stage, same-sector comparables yields a $2.3B median valuation, with a range spanning $2.0B (d-Matrix) to $11.0B (SambaNova Systems). Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied due to absence of target revenue disclosure, a standard limitation for early-stage private companies.\n\nThe triangulation yields a range of $221M to $2.7B, with a median of $1.3B across both applicable methods. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty in relative positioning within the peer set: SambaNova's $11B valuation significantly exceeds the lower-priced peers, suggesting valuation outcomes depend heavily on SiPearl's demonstrated technical differentiation, go-to-market traction, and capital efficiency relative to this comparison universe. Additional data on revenue run-rate or customer concentration would narrow this range materially.",
