      "narrative": "Fractile is a Series B semiconductor company that has raised $220M to date. Valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 8 private peers in chips and semiconductors at similar or adjacent stages\u2014including SambaNova Systems ($11.0B, Series A), Rebellions ($2.3B, Series A), d-Matrix ($2.0B, Series A), Positron AI ($1.0B, Series B), and DEEPX ($529M, Series C)\u2014alongside 3 public semiconductor benchmarks (ALAB, NVDA, AMD).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x multiplier to the $220M total raised as a proxy for base value, implying $418M. Peer-median anchoring across the 5-company private comparable set yields a median valuation of $2.0B, with a range from $529M to $11.0B. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiple (20.5x median across public semis) cannot be applied due to the absence of Fractile's revenue disclosure, typical for private companies at this stage.\n\nTriangulation of the two applicable methods supports a valuation range of $355M (low) to $2.3B (high), with a median of $1.2B. The wide range reflects material variance between stage-progression and peer-median approaches, and the substantial dispersion within the peer set itself\u2014driven largely by SambaNova's outlier valuation. Key uncertainties include Fractile's revenue trajectory relative to peers and the appropriate stage-adjustment factor for Series B in this capital-intensive sector.",
