      "narrative": "HIMERA is a Seed-stage defense & security company founded by Misha Rudominsky and Oleksiy Oliynyk that has raised $2.5M+. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 10 comparable companies\u20142 public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms including UFORCE, Anduril Industries, Helsing, Shield AI, and Saronic\u2014spanning Seed and Series A stages within Defense & Security.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression modeling uses the $2.5M raised as a proxy for current value and applies a 2.5x multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage advancement, implying $6.25M. Peer-median analysis examines five same-sector comparables across adjacent stages: UFORCE ($1.0B, Seed), Stark Defence ($4.0B, Series A), Castelion ($1.0B, Series A), Singularity ($400M, Series A), and NODA AI ($125M, Series A). The median valuation across this set is $1.0B, with a range spanning $125M to $4.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis yields a low estimate of $5.3M, median of $503M, and high of $1.1B. The wide dispersion reflects two material uncertainties: the extreme variance in Defense & Security peer valuations (80x spread from floor to ceiling) and the limited visibility into HIMERA's technical progress, customer traction, and defensibility relative to the peer set. Stage-progression suggests a conservative floor, while peer comparables anchor the upper bound, though the sector's valuation heterogeneity requires careful underwriting of product-market fit and competitive positioning before final valuation assignment.",
