      "narrative": "Harmattan AI is a Series B defense and security technology company founded by Mouad M'Ghari and Martin de Gourcuff, currently valued at $1.4B post-money following $200M in total capital raised. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 10 companies\u20142 public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private\u2014all operating in the Defense & Security sector at similar stages.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier to the $1.4B last post-money valuation, yielding $2.7B and reflecting typical expansion-stage progression. Peer-median analysis across five same-sector, same-stage comparables\u2014Dream Security ($3.0B), Code Metal ($1.2B), Defense Unicorns ($1.0B), Heven AeroTech ($1.0B), and TurbineOne ($300M)\u2014produces a median valuation of $1.0B, with a range spanning $300M to $3.0B.\n\nTriangulating these two methods produces a median valuation of $1.8B, with a plausible range from $850M (conservative floor) to $3.1B (upside case). The current $1.4B valuation sits below the median, reflecting either relative undervaluation relative to peer cohort medians or near-term funding momentum. Key uncertainties include revenue traction relative to peer benchmarks, defensibility of the technology platform within a crowded defense-tech landscape, and customer concentration risk in government contracting.",
