      "narrative": "Cailabs is a Series C space & aerospace company that has raised \u20ac57M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 6 private peers at the same or adjacent stage (Sierra Space, Apex Space, Cowboy Space Corporation, Varda Space Industries, Aalyria, and one additional peer), alongside 5 public space & aerospace companies (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) that anchor sector multiples at a 27.4x median P/S.\n\nTwo quantitative methods proved applicable. The stage-progression method applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement, yielding $97M on the $57M total-raised proxy. The peer-median approach anchors to the $1.8B median valuation across 6 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private comparables, with a range of $1.15B to $8.0B. Public-comp P/S anchoring cannot be applied without revenue disclosure, which is unavailable for this private company.\n\nTriangulation of the two applicable methods produces a valuation range of $82M (low) to $2.1B (high), with a median of $943M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around Cailabs' revenue scale and profitability trajectory relative to the peer set. The peer-median result ($1.8B) notably exceeds the stage-progression result ($97M), suggesting either that Cailabs commands premium positioning within its cohort or that the raised-capital proxy substantially understates true enterprise value. Key uncertainties include undisclosed revenue, unit economics, and technology differentiation relative to the cited peer sample.",
