      "narrative": "Sateliot is a Series B-stage space & aerospace company that has raised \u20ac70M+. The valuation analysis triangulates across a comparable universe of 5 public tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers, with 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables directly informing the quantitative methods.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis uses the $70M total raised as a proxy base and applies a 1.9x multiplier typical for Series B advancement, yielding $133M. Peer-median analysis across four same-sector comparables\u2014Sierra Space ($8.0B, Series C), Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B, Series B), Aalyria ($1.3B, Series B), and Skyryse ($1.1B, Series C)\u2014produces a median valuation of $1.6B, with a range of $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (27.4x median across the sector) cannot be applied absent disclosed revenue for Sateliot.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $113M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $892M. The wide dispersion\u2014driven largely by the peer-median method's dependence on stage-adjacent but materially larger businesses\u2014reflects meaningful uncertainty around market positioning and growth trajectory. The stage-progression method yields substantially lower figures, suggesting reliance on peer comparables carries material weight in this valuation. Key uncertainties include Sateliot's revenue scale relative to sampled peers and the appropriateness of Series C comps for a Series B business.",
