      "narrative": "Ephos is a seed-stage semiconductor company that has raised \u20ac41.5M in EU funding plus $8.5M in seed capital. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 11 private peers (including SambaNova Systems, Rebellions, and d-Matrix) and 3 public semiconductor benchmarks (ALAB, NVDA, AMD).\n\nTwo triangulation methods prove applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of seed-to-next-stage advancement to the $42M raised proxy, implying a $104M valuation. Peer-median anchoring across three same-sector, same-stage private comparables yields a $2.3B median valuation, with a range of $2.0B to $11.0B. Public-comp P/S anchoring is not applicable: while the semiconductor sector median trades at 20.5x revenue across the three public tickers, Ephos's revenue remains undisclosed, precluding this method.\n\nThe two applicable methods generate a wide implied range: $88M (conservative), $1.2B (median), and $2.7B (high). This spread reflects the tension between stage-based mechanics (suggesting ~$104M) and peer-comparable valuations anchored to Series A stage comparables. Key uncertainties include Ephos's actual revenue run-rate, capital efficiency relative to peers, and the specific technology differentiation that would justify positioning within the $2.0B\u2013$11.0B peer range versus the lower stage-progression anchor.",
