      "narrative": "Synspective is a publicly listed Space & Aerospace company founded by Motoyuki Arai, having raised approximately $220M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 4 same-sector, same-stage peers: Rocket Lab ($40.0B), Planet Labs ($7.6B), Firefly Aerospace ($2.9B), and Astroscale ($840M).\n\nThe peer-median method is the primary applicable approach, anchored to the median valuation of $5.2B across the four comparable companies. This method is appropriate given Synspective's publicly traded status and direct comparability to listed Space & Aerospace operators. The peer universe spans a wide range\u2014from $840M at the low end (Astroscale) to $40.0B at the high end (Rocket Lab)\u2014reflecting material heterogeneity in scale and business model within the sector. A Public-Comp Anchoring approach using Price-to-Sales multiples (sector median 27.4x across 6 public tickers) cannot be applied due to absence of target revenue disclosure.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is supported by the single applicable method, suggesting a median valuation of $5.2B with a range of $4.4B to $6.0B. Key uncertainties include the wide dispersion in peer valuations, which reflects differentiated market positioning within Space & Aerospace, and the lack of revenue-based validation. Relative positioning within the peer set depends critically on Synspective's revenue trajectory, operational maturity, and contract backlog\u2014factors not quantified in available data.",
