      "narrative": "Sagar Defence Engineering, a Series A-stage defense & security company, has raised $25.4M to date. The valuation assessment draws from a peer universe of 10 comparable companies: 2 public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private entities including Stark Defence, Castelion, Singularity, NODA AI, and Anduril Industries, all operating in the same sector and development stage.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-Progression methodology uses the $25M raised as a valuation proxy and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A advancement, yielding an implied valuation of $51M. Peer-Median analysis across four same-sector, same-stage comparables produces a median valuation of $700M, derived from a range spanning $125M (NODA AI) to $4.0B (Stark Defence). The median reflects substantial dispersion within the peer set, with an interquartile distribution from $400M to $1.0B.\n\nTriangulating these two methods produces a low-to-high valuation range of $43M to $805M, with a median of $375M. The wide band reflects asymmetric peer valuations and early-stage uncertainty inherent in frontier defense technology. Key uncertainties include relative technology maturity versus listed peers, customer concentration and contract visibility, and regulatory pathway clarity within defense procurement. The $375M midpoint should be weighted against the Stage-Progression result ($51M) as a more conservative anchor given limited operational data at Series A.",
