      "narrative": "SatSure is a Series B-stage Space & Aerospace company. Valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 4 same-sector peers at Series B and Series C stages: Sierra Space ($8.0B, Series C), Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B, Series B), Aalyria ($1.3B, Series B), and Skyryse ($1.1B, Series C).\n\nThe peer-median method is the primary applicable framework. The median valuation across these four comparables stands at $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.1B to $8.0B. This range reflects heterogeneity in stage maturity and market positioning within the cohort. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (sector median 27.4x across 5 public tickers including RKLB, LUNR, and ASTS) is not applicable due to unavailable revenue data for the target.\n\nTriangulation yields a central estimate of $1.6B with a defensible range of $1.4B\u2013$1.9B. Key uncertainties include revenue scale (undisclosed), capital efficiency relative to peers, and the wide valuation dispersion at Series C (Sierra Space at $8.0B versus Skyryse at $1.1B), which suggests material differences in traction or market perception among comparable-stage operators. The narrow methodological base (one applicable method) argues for caution and underscores the value of updated financial metrics and customer concentration data.",
