      "narrative": "Lohum Cleantech is a Series C climate and energy company founded by Rajat Verma that has raised $87.7M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of three same-sector, same-stage private comparables (KoBold Metals at $3.0B, Electric Hydrogen at $1.0B, and Amogy at $700M), alongside a broader universe of nine frontier-climate peers including Redwood Materials and QuantumScape, with one public reference point (LNZA).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. The stage-progression method applies a typical Series C step-up multiplier of 1.7x to the $88M raised proxy, yielding $149M. The peer-median method benchmarks against the three same-stage, same-sector comparables, which show a median valuation of $1.0B with a range of $700M to $3.0B. The peer-median approach accounts for the fact that later-stage climate-tech companies in this cohort command substantially higher valuations than early funding levels would suggest.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a range of $127M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $575M. The wide spread reflects meaningful uncertainty: the stage-progression method anchors conservatively near cumulative capital, while the peer-median method reflects market pricing for comparable risk and stage. Key uncertainties include unit economics at scale, technology differentiation relative to KoBold and Redwood, and near-term capital efficiency relative to peer burn profiles.",
