      "narrative": "Hypersonix Launch Systems is a Series A defense and security company that has raised $46M AUD to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer universe of 10 comparable companies\u20142 public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private entities\u2014operating in the same sector and stage. The private peer set includes Stark Defence, Castelion, Singularity, NODA AI, and Anduril Industries.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression methodology, using the $46M raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x multiplier typical for Series A advancement, implies a valuation of $92M. Peer-median analysis across four same-sector, same-stage comparables yields a $700M median valuation. This peer cohort spans a wide range\u2014from $125M (NODA AI) to $4.0B (Stark Defence)\u2014reflecting significant dispersion in the defense-tech market at this stage.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $78M (low) to $805M (high), with a median of $396M. The wide spread between stage-progression and peer-median methods reflects two distinct valuation regimes: early-stage funding multiples versus market-determined peer valuations in a heterogeneous sector. Key uncertainties include the composition and transaction recency of the peer set, the degree to which Hypersonix's technology and market traction align with outlier peers like Stark Defence, and sector-specific factors (regulatory environment, customer concentration) that drive the observed valuation dispersion.",
