      "narrative": "Classiq is a Series C quantum computing software company that has raised $200M+ to date. The broader quantum computing sector comprises 3 public companies (IONQ, RGTI, QBTS) and 8 private peers including Quantinuum, IonQ, PsiQuantum, D-Wave Quantum, and SandboxAQ.\n\nStage-progression analysis applies directly to Classiq's valuation. Using the $200M total raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical for Series C to subsequent-stage progression yields an implied valuation of $340M. This method is appropriate given the absence of sufficient narrow-set peer comparables\u2014while 8 same-sector peers exist, none satisfy the minimum threshold of three datapoints when filtered by stage or valuation tier. A peer-median approach therefore cannot be reliably applied.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $289M (low) to $391M (high), with a median of $340M. This range reflects the single applicable method and carries meaningful uncertainty. The quantum computing sector remains nascent with limited public trading history and heterogeneous business models across hardware, software, and service layers, which constrains confidence in traditional comparables. The valuation is sensitive to assumptions about when Classiq will achieve meaningful enterprise adoption and revenue scale relative to the capital deployed.",
