      "narrative": "Majestic Labs is a Series A-stage semiconductor company founded by Ofer Shacham, Sha Rabii, and Masumi Reynders, having raised over $100M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 3 public semiconductor firms (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private peers across chips and semiconductors, with particular focus on 3 same-stage private comparables: SambaNova Systems ($11.0B), Rebellions ($2.3B), and d-Matrix ($2.0B).\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis anchors to the $100M total raised and applies a typical 2.0x step-up multiplier from Series A to the next stage, implying a $200M valuation. Peer-median analysis across the 3 same-sector, same-stage comparables yields a median valuation of $2.3B, with a range of $2.0B to $11.0B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied absent disclosed revenue figures. The wide dispersion in peer valuations\u2014driven largely by SambaNova's $11.0B outlier versus the $2.0B\u2013$2.3B median\u2014reflects material uncertainty in market pricing for early-stage semiconductor hardware.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a range of $170M (low) to $2.7B (high), with a median implied value of $1.3B across both applicable methods. The key uncertainty is whether Majestic's technology, team, or market position aligns with the lower quartile peers or the broader median cluster. Additional diligence on IP differentiation, design wins, and capital efficiency would refine this range.",
