      "narrative": "Hailo is a Series D semiconductor chip design company that has raised $564M+ to date. The valuation analysis triangulates across a peer set of 4 private companies at the same or adjacent stage\u2014Etched ($5.0B, Series E), Ayar Labs ($3.8B, Series E), Tenstorrent ($2.7B, Series D), and DEEPX ($529M, Series C)\u2014plus reference to 3 public semiconductor comparables (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) where applicable.\n\nTwo quantitative methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $564M total raised as a baseline proxy and applies a typical 1.5x multiplier for Series D-to-next-stage advancement, yielding $846M. Peer-median analysis anchors to the $3.2B median valuation across the 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage peers (range: $529M\u2013$5.0B). Public-comp anchoring via price-to-sales multiples (median 20.5x across the three public semiconductors) is not applicable due to absence of disclosed revenue for the target.\n\nThe triangulation supports a range of $719M (low) to $3.7B (high), with a median of $2.0B. The stage-progression method biases toward the lower bound, while peer-median anchoring toward the upper range reflects Hailo's proximity to Series E comparables. Key uncertainties include the absence of revenue disclosure (preventing P/S calibration to public comps) and significant valuation dispersion within the peer set, reflecting heterogeneity in chip architecture, market focus, and progress toward commercialization.",
