      "narrative": "H2Pro is a Series B climate and energy company that has raised over $100M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 9 private and 1 public company operating in frontier energy and materials technology, including peers such as KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Amogy.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised of $100M as a proxy and applying a typical Series B step-up multiplier of 1.9x, implies a valuation of $190M. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014KoBold Metals at $3.0B, Electric Hydrogen at $1.0B, and Amogy at $700M\u2014yields a median valuation of $1.0B, with a range of $700M to $3.0B. The marked divergence reflects heterogeneity in capital intensity and commercialization timing within the climate-tech segment.\n\nTriangulating these two methods produces a valuation range of $162M to $1.1B, with a median of $595M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around H2Pro's technology maturity, path to commercialization, and capital requirements relative to peers. Stage-progression suggests the low end; peer multiples suggest substantially higher value. Resolution of execution risk and clarity on near-term milestones would be critical to narrowing this band.",
