      "narrative": "NordSpace is a Series A stage space and aerospace company founded by Rahul Goel that has raised $38M+ to date. The valuation assessment triangulates across a comp universe of five public Space & Aerospace companies (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and eight private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, ICEYE, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs.\n\nTwo valuation methods proved applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, using the $38M raised as a proxy floor, yielding $76M. Peer-median anchoring across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B Series B), Aalyria ($1.3B Series B), and Starcloud ($1.1B Seed)\u2014produces a $1.3B median with a $1.1B\u2013$2.0B range. Public-comp anchoring was not applicable; while the Space & Aerospace sector median P/S ratio is 27.4x across the five public tickers, NordSpace's revenue is not on file, precluding price-to-sales application.\n\nTriangulation across the two applicable methods supports a valuation range of $65M (low) to $1.5B (high), with a median of $688M. The wide dispersion reflects the stage and comparability tension: the stage-progression floor anchors to capital deployed, while peer medians skew upward given the maturity of the reference set. Key uncertainties include revenue trajectory and competitive positioning relative to the named peers, neither of which the available data clarifies.",
