      "narrative": "Wyvern is a Series A-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $16M to date. Valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 5 public tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 3 private peers at same or adjacent stage: Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B, Series B), Aalyria ($1.3B, Series B), and Starcloud ($1.1B, Seed).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement to the $16M raised proxy, yielding $32M. Peer-median anchoring uses the median valuation of three same-sector peers: $1.3B, with a range spanning $1.1B to $2.0B. Public-comp P/S anchoring cannot be applied, as Wyvern's revenue is not disclosed.\n\nThe two applicable methods produce a valuation range of $27M (low) to $1.5B (high), with a median estimate of $666M. The wide dispersion reflects structural tension between stage-based approaches, which anchor to capital deployed, and peer-median methods, which reflect market pricing for later-stage competitors. Key uncertainties include the timing and magnitude of revenue ramp, Wyvern's specific technical differentiation relative to the peer set, and overall sector appetite for frontier aerospace at the Series A-to-B transition.",
