      "narrative": "OroraTech is a Series B space and aerospace company that has raised \u20ac38M to date. Valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 5 public peers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private companies in the same sector and stage, including Cowboy Space Corporation, Aalyria, and Skyryse.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement to the \u20ac38M raised proxy, yielding \u20ac72M implied value. Peer-median analysis across four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Sierra Space ($8.0B Series C), Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B Series B), Aalyria ($1.3B Series B), and Skyryse ($1.1B Series C)\u2014produces a median valuation of \u20ac1.65B, with a range of \u20ac1.15B to \u20ac8.0B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied; the Space & Aerospace sector median P/S is 27.4x across 6 public tickers, but OroraTech's revenue is not disclosed.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a range of \u20ac61M to \u20ac1.9B, with a median of \u20ac861M. This wide spread reflects material uncertainty around growth trajectory and technology validation. The stage-progression method yields a floor; peer medians suggest substantially higher value, though comparables themselves span an order of magnitude. Key uncertainties include revenue run-rate, customer traction, and whether peer valuations reflect market peak or sustainable fundamentals in the space sector.",
