      "narrative": "Corintis is a Series A semiconductor company that has raised $25M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 3 public semiconductor players (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private peers, with particular focus on 3 same-stage, same-sector private comparables: SambaNova Systems ($11.0B), Rebellions ($2.3B), and d-Matrix ($2.0B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised as a proxy for current value, applies a typical 2.0x step-up multiplier from Series A to next stage, yielding $50M. Peer-median analysis across the 3 same-stage semiconductor companies implies $2.3B, with a range of $2.0B to $11.0B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied, as Corintis does not publicly disclose revenue; the public semiconductor median P/S of 20.5x therefore remains inapplicable without this figure.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $42M (low) to $2.7B (high), with a median of $1.2B. The wide dispersion reflects meaningful uncertainty: stage-progression suggests a floor near $50M based on capital deployment, while peer-median methodology is dominated by SambaNova's outlier valuation at $11.0B, which pulls the upper bound substantially. Resolution of this range would benefit from clearer visibility into Corintis's technology differentiation relative to Rebellions and d-Matrix, the tighter peer cluster at $2.0B\u2013$2.3B.",
