      "narrative": "Causaly is a Series B biotech and health software company that has raised $95M to date. The valuation analysis employs two applicable triangulation methods against a peer set comprising 4 private companies in the same sector and stage (Colossal Biosciences at $10.3B, Chai Discovery at $3.8B, New Limit at $3.1B, and Eikon Therapeutics at $539M) alongside 3 public biotech comparables (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L).\n\nStage-progression methodology applies a 1.9x multiplier to the $95M total raised proxy, yielding an implied valuation of $180M. This reflects typical capital step-up patterns from Series B to subsequent rounds. The peer-median method yields $3.5B, the median across the 4 private comps with a range spanning $539M to $10.3B. Public-comp anchoring is not applicable owing to the absence of Causaly's revenue disclosure. The two applicable methods produce a triangulated range of $153M (low) to $4.0B (high), with a median of $1.8B.\n\nKey uncertainties include significant dispersion within the peer set\u2014a 19x spread between minimum and maximum valuations\u2014and reliance on stage-progression from limited raised capital as a proxy absent disclosed financials. The wide range reflects genuine heterogeneity in biotech valuations at this stage rather than methodological weakness. Resolution would benefit from revenue visibility and clearer stage alignment among peers.",
