      "narrative": "Hexana is a Seed-stage nuclear energy company founded by Sylvain Nizou and Paul Gauthe that has raised \u20ac25M to date. The valuation analysis is informed by a comp universe of 11 peers across nuclear energy\u20143 public companies (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 8 private firms including Nano Nuclear Energy, Helion, Oklo, Valar Atomics, and X-Energy\u2014though the private nuclear energy subset lacks sufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables for robust peer-median benchmarking.\n\nGiven data constraints, the analysis relies on stage-progression methodology, which applies a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage advancement. Using the \u20ac25M total raised as a valuation proxy, this approach yields an implied valuation of \u20ac62M. A sensitivity framework around this single method\u2014incorporating downside and upside scenarios\u2014produces a triangulated range of \u20ac53M (low), \u20ac62M (median), and \u20ac72M (high). The stage-progression result sits squarely within this band.\n\nThe primary limitation is the absence of a sufficiently dense peer cohort at the same stage and valuation tier. The nuclear energy sector remains fragmented across development phases and technology approaches, constraining cross-company comparability. A Seed valuation of \u20ac62M is defensible on stage mechanics alone, but this estimate should be revisited as additional private-market nuclear transactions and Hexana's own operational milestones emerge.",
