      "narrative": "Scout Space is a Series A frontier-tech company in Space & Aerospace founded by Eric Ingram and Sergio Gallucci, with $18M raised to date. The sector comp universe includes 5 public companies (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) trading at a median 27.4x P/S, and a private peer set anchored by SpaceX, Rocket Lab, ICEYE, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using the $18M total raised as a proxy baseline and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A progression, implies a $36M valuation. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B Series B), Aalyria ($1.3B Series B), and Starcloud ($1.1B Seed)\u2014yields a $1.3B median with a $1.1B\u2013$2.0B range. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied without Scout Space's revenue, which remains undisclosed.\n\nThe triangulated analysis yields a $31M\u2013$1.5B range with a median of $668M across two methods. The extreme spread reflects substantial stage and maturity variance within the peer set; the stage-progression floor assumes minimal capital efficiency gain, while the peer-median ceiling reflects comparables further along their growth trajectory. Key uncertainties include Scout Space's revenue trajectory, capital efficiency relative to peers, and the appropriate discount or premium for stage positioning versus the Series B/Seed comparables used.",
