      "narrative": "Genesis Therapeutics is a Series B-stage biotech company that has raised $280M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 4 private peers in Biotech & Health at Series B/C stage, supplemented by 3 public-sector reference points (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L). The private peer set includes Eikon Therapeutics ($539M), New Limit ($3.1B), Chai Discovery ($3.8B), and Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement to the $280M raised baseline, implying a $532M valuation. Peer-median analysis anchors to the four same-sector comparables, which have a median valuation of $3.5B (range: $539M\u2013$10.3B). Public-comp anchoring via price-to-sales multiples cannot be applied because Genesis's revenue is not disclosed. The wide dispersion in peer valuations\u2014driven by heterogeneous technology maturity and capital efficiency\u2014creates substantial uncertainty.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $452M (low) to $4.0B (high), with a median of $2.0B. The low end reflects conservative stage-based progression; the high end incorporates the upper quartile of peer multiples. Key uncertainties include Genesis's unreported revenue, R&D productivity relative to peers, and timeline to next funding milestone. The $2.0B median represents a 6.4x step-up from total raised, consistent with late Series B positioning but materially below the highest-valuation peers.",
