      "narrative": "BRINC Drones, a Series C-stage defense and security drone manufacturer founded by Blake Resnick, has raised $157M to date. The valuation analysis triangulates across a peer set of 12 same-sector and adjacent-stage companies, including 8 private firms (Quantum-Systems, Helsing, Saronic, Anduril Industries, Shield AI, Neros, Chaos Industries, Dream Security) and 2 public comparables (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS), with peer valuations ranging from $300M to $18.0B.\n\nTwo methods are applicable. Stage-progression applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement to the $157M raised proxy, implying a valuation of $267M. Peer-median analysis across the 12-company cohort yields a median valuation of $2.3B, substantially higher, reflecting the sector's capital intensity and venture appetite for frontier-defense capabilities. The peer range ($300M\u2013$18.0B) reflects significant dispersion, with later-stage comparables (Helsing at $18.0B, Saronic at $9.2B) at the upper bound and earlier-stage peers anchoring lower.\n\nThe triangulated range is $227M (low) to $2.7B (high), with a median of $1.3B. Stage-progression supports the lower bound; peer-median anchors the upper bound. Key uncertainties include BRINC's product maturity and customer concentration relative to peers, capital efficiency relative to the wider cohort, and whether the peer set's heterogeneity (spanning Series B through Series D) adequately reflects BRINC's position within the sequence.",
