      "narrative": "Sagence is a Series B semiconductor company founded by Vishal Sarin that has raised $58M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 8 private peers in frontier chip design and 3 public semiconductor benchmarks (ALAB, NVDA, AMD), with notable private comparables including Positron AI ($1.0B, Series B), SambaNova Systems ($11.0B, Series A), and Rebellions ($2.3B, Series A).\n\nTwo triangulation methods apply here. Stage-progression analysis uses the $58M total raised as a valuation proxy and applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement, yielding $110M. Peer-median anchoring across the 5 most relevant same-sector and same/adjacent-stage companies produces $2.0B, with a distribution spanning $529M (DEEPX, Series C) to $11.0B (SambaNova, Series A). Public-comp P/S anchoring cannot be applied: while the public semiconductor sector trades at a 20.5x price-to-sales median, Sagence's revenue is not disclosed, preventing the calculation.\n\nThe triangulation supports a valuation range of $94M to $2.3B, with a median of $1.1B across the two applicable methods. The wide spread reflects genuine uncertainty in the private frontier-chip market, where stage and specific technical differentiation drive outsized valuation dispersion. The peer-median method suggests valuations in the $1.0B\u2013$2.3B band appear defensible for Series B positioning; stage-progression alone likely understates value given the sector's current capital intensity and technical risk premiums.",
