      "narrative": "Performance Drone Works is a Series B-stage defense and security company that has raised $110M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 10 peers (2 public, 8 private) operating within the Defense & Security sector at equivalent or proximate stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $110M total raised as a baseline proxy and applies a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B advancement, implying a valuation of $209M. Peer-median analysis identifies six same-sector, same-stage comparables\u2014Dream Security ($3.0B), Harmattan AI ($1.4B), Code Metal ($1.2B), Defense Unicorns ($1.0B), Heven AeroTech ($1.0B), and one additional peer\u2014yielding a median valuation of $1.1B with a range spanning $300M to $3.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis across both methods supports a valuation range of $178M (low) to $1.3B (high), with a median estimate of $667M. The wide range reflects material uncertainty around comparable company selection and stage-specific risk adjustments within the Defense & Security sector. The peer-median method carries greater weight given the size and relevance of the comparable set, though meaningful divergence between stage-progression and peer outcomes warrants scrutiny of whether Performance Drone Works' traction and market position align with established peer valuations or warrant positioning toward the range extremes.",
