      "narrative": "Deep Sentinel is a Series B-stage defense and security company founded by David Selinger that has raised $55M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of 10 comparable companies\u20142 public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms\u2014all operating in the Defense & Security sector at similar or equivalent stages. The private peer universe includes Dream Security, Harmattan AI, Code Metal, Defense Unicorns, and Heven AeroTech, among others.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis used the $55M total raised as a proxy for current value and applied a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement, yielding $104M. Peer-median analysis examined 6 same-sector, same-stage comparables with valuations spanning $300M to $3.0B; the median across this set stands at $1.1B. The wide dispersion reflects heterogeneity in market position and investor appetite within the defense tech category.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $89M (low) to $1.3B (high), with a median of $615M. The gap between stage-progression ($104M) and peer-median ($1.1B) suggests material uncertainty around Deep Sentinel's competitive positioning relative to named peers. Key uncertainties include revenue traction, customer concentration, and whether the company's technology or go-to-market capability justifies valuations clustering above $1B versus the implied $89M\u2013$104M floor derived from capital deployed.",
