      "narrative": "CesiumAstro is a Series C-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $470M to date. Valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of six same-sector peers at Series B through Series D stages, alongside five public space and aerospace equities (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.7x multiplier typical of Series C advancement, yielding an implied valuation of $799M based on the $470M raised proxy. Peer-median anchoring references six private space companies at comparable or adjacent stages\u2014Sierra Space ($8.0B), Apex Space ($2.3B), Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B), Varda Space Industries ($1.6B), Aalyria ($1.3B), and one additional peer\u2014producing a median valuation of $1.8B with a range of $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp multiples cannot be applied due to absence of target revenue disclosure, typical for private companies. The median public Space & Aerospace sector trades at 27.4x price-to-sales.\n\nThe two applicable methods triangulate to a range of $679M (low) to $2.1B (high), with a median of $1.3B. This range reflects meaningful dispersion driven by heterogeneity within the peer set, particularly the $8.0B Sierra Space outlier. Key uncertainties include stage-specific capital efficiency relative to peer cohort and revenue trajectory relative to capital deployed.",
