      "narrative": "Loft Orbital is a Series C space and aerospace company that has raised $326M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of 6 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private companies (Sierra Space at $8.0B, Apex Space at $2.3B, Cowboy Space Corporation at $2.0B, Varda Space Industries at $1.6B, Aalyria at $1.3B, and one additional peer) alongside 5 public comparables in Space & Aerospace (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL).\n\nTwo valuation methods prove applicable. The Stage-Progression method, applying a typical 1.7x Series C step-up multiplier to the $326M raised proxy, implies $554M. The Peer-Median approach uses the 6-company private comparable set, yielding a median valuation of $1.8B with a range spanning $1.1B to $8.0B. The Public-Comp Anchoring method is inapplicable due to absence of target revenue data, though the sector P/S median stands at 27.4x across the five public tickers.\n\nTriangulating the two applicable methods produces a low-to-high range of $471M to $2.1B, with a median implied valuation of $1.2B. The wide spread reflects material uncertainty around Loft Orbital's positioning within its peer cohort\u2014particularly relative to higher-valued Series C and D stage competitors. Key uncertainties include target revenue traction, addressable market capture, and technical execution against incumbent aerospace players.",
