      "narrative": "Vector Defense is a Series A defense and security company that has raised $61M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of 4 same-sector, same-stage private companies (Stark Defence, Castelion, Singularity, and NODA AI) with valuations ranging from $125M to $4.0B, plus reference to 2 public comparables and 8 additional private frontier-defense firms including Anduril Industries.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression, using the $61M total raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, implies a valuation of $122M. Peer-median analysis across the 4 same-sector Series A companies yields a median valuation of $700M, with a range of $125M\u2013$4.0B. The wide peer dispersion reflects heterogeneity in progress and market timing within frontier defense, though the median is supported by at least two companies at or above that level.\n\nTriangulation across both methods produces a valuation range of $104M (low) to $805M (high), with a median of $411M. The analysis suggests Vector Defense most likely falls in the $300M\u2013$700M band, pending resolution of key uncertainties around revenue traction, customer concentration, and technical differentiation relative to the peer cohort. The substantial variance between stage-progression and peer-median anchors reflects limited visibility into Vector's operational maturity relative to named comparables.",
