      "narrative": "Voya Energy is a Seed-stage climate and energy company founded by Richard Wang, Matt Horton, and Steven Kaye that has raised $13M to date. The broader Climate & Energy sector comprises one public comparable (ticker: LNZA) and eight private peers including Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Enovix. However, the peer set lacks sufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables within a tight valuation band to support a median-multiple approach\u2014no subset of three or more peers met the filtering criteria.\n\nConsequently, valuation relies on stage-progression methodology applied to the $13M raised as a proxy for current implied value. Using a typical Seed-to-next-stage step-up multiplier of 2.5x yields an implied valuation of $32M. This represents the primary quantitative anchor for the analysis, as peer median comps are not applicable given data sparsity.\n\nThe triangulation supports a valuation range of $28M (low) to $37M (high), with a central estimate of $32M. The width of this range reflects reliance on a single applicable method; key uncertainties include whether Voya's pre-Seed economics will sustain the 2.5x multiplier typical of the broader frontier tech cohort, and whether emerging private market comparables in advanced materials or energy hardware will provide tighter peer anchoring in future funding rounds.",
