      "narrative": "Cartesia is a Series B-stage AI & Software company that has raised $186M to date. Valuation analysis relies on a peer set of 4 same-sector, same-stage comparables: Scale AI ($29.0B), Physical Intelligence ($5.6B), Black Forest Labs ($3.2B), and Field AI ($2.0B), supplemented by public software comparables including Palantir (PLTR).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $186M in total capital raised as a valuation proxy, applying a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement, yielding $353M. Peer-median valuation identifies the median across the 4 same-stage, same-sector comparables at $4.4B, with a range spanning $2.0B to $29.0B. The wide spread reflects meaningful heterogeneity within frontier AI\u2014particularly the outlier positioning of Scale AI relative to the tighter clustering of Physical Intelligence, Black Forest Labs, and Field AI around $2B\u2013$5.6B.\n\nThe two methods produce divergent signals, with stage-progression implying $353M and peer-median implying $4.4B. Triangulation across these approaches supports a valuation range of $300M (low) to $5.1B (high), with a median of $2.4B. The significant spread reflects two material uncertainties: the applicability of raised capital as a valuation proxy for early-stage frontier tech, and the degree to which Cartesia's product traction and market position align with the broader peer distribution rather than outlier cases like Scale AI.",
