      "narrative": "Traysar is a Seed-stage Defense & Security company that has raised $25M to date. The relevant peer universe comprises 10 private companies and 2 public comparables in the same sector at Seed and Series A stages, including UFORCE, Anduril Industries, Helsing, Shield AI, and Saronic.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-Progression methodology, using total capital raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical for Seed-to-next-stage advancement, implies a valuation of $62M. Peer-Median methodology surveyed five same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Stark Defence ($4.0B Series A), UFORCE ($1.0B Seed), Castelion ($1.0B Series A), Singularity ($400M Series A), and NODA AI ($125M Series A)\u2014yielding a median valuation of $1.0B, with a peer range spanning $125M to $4.0B.\n\nThe two-method triangulation supports a valuation range of $53M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $531M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty in peer selection: Traysar's position relative to early-stage pure-play defense tech (UFORCE at $1.0B) versus mature Series A operators (NODA AI at $125M) remains undefined. Stage positioning, product maturity, and customer traction relative to the peer set are critical vectors for narrowing this range.",
