      "narrative": "Generalist AI is a Series B robotics and manufacturing company led by former DeepMind principals (CEO Pete Florence, Chief Scientist Andy Zeng, CTO Andrew Barry). The target's current post-money valuation stands at $2.0B following $500M+ raised to date. The comparable universe consists of 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private peers\u2014Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B Series B), Agile Robots ($1.0B Series C), and Nimble Robotics ($1.0B Series C)\u2014plus 1 public comparable and 8 additional private robotics firms.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B to Series C advancement, yielding $3.8B. Peer-median analysis across the 4-company comparable set yields $1.3B, with a range of $1.0B to $1.8B, reflecting broader market positioning. The peer-median method implies the target is priced above recent cohort medians, consistent with founder pedigree and capital deployed.\n\nTriangulation across both methods supports a valuation range of $1.1B (floor) to $4.4B (ceiling), with a median estimate of $2.6B. The target's current $2.0B valuation sits within this band, near the lower-median. Key uncertainties include execution risk on product-market fit, competitive positioning relative to the expanding robotics startup ecosystem, and sustainability of stage-typical valuation multiples in a maturing sector.",
