      "narrative": "Nudge is a Series A biotech & health company founded by Fred Ehrsam (Coinbase, Paradigm co-founder), Quintin Frerichs, and Jeremy Barenholtz (ex-Neuralink VP). The company has raised $100M to date. The valuation universe comprises 3 public comparables (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private peers including Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, and Recursion Pharmaceuticals.\n\nGiven data constraints, only the stage-progression method is applicable. Using the $100M total raised as a baseline proxy and applying a typical 2.0x Series A step-up multiplier yields an implied valuation of $200M. Peer-median triangulation is inapplicable\u2014while 7 same-sector companies exist, none yield the minimum 3 datapoints required at the same stage, adjacent stage, or similar valuation tier. Public-comp anchoring cannot be executed because the target's revenue is not disclosed, a standard limitation with private companies.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $170M\u2013$230M, centered at $200M. This range reflects the single applicable method's output and typical variance bounds. Key uncertainties include the absence of same-stage comparable pricing and undisclosed financial metrics (revenue, burn rate, milestones). A more robust triangulation would require either disclosed revenue figures or access to additional Series A biotech transactions at similar scale and stage. Investors should view this as a preliminary framework pending fuller disclosure.",
