      "narrative": "Paradromics is a Series B-stage biotech company founded by Matt Angle, with total capital raised of approximately $90\u2013120M plus ~$18M in non-dilutive government funding (NIH/DARPA). The valuation analysis draws from a peer universe of 4 private companies in biotech & health at Series B/C stages, alongside 3 public biotech comparables (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B advancement to the $90M raised baseline, implying a valuation of $171M. Peer-median analysis across four same-sector, same-stage companies (Eikon Therapeutics at $539M, New Limit at $3.1B, Chai Discovery at $3.8B, Colossal Biosciences at $10.3B) yields a median of $3.5B, though the wide range ($539M\u2013$10.3B) reflects material heterogeneity. Public-comp anchoring via price-to-sales multiples (median 9.2x across the three public tickers) cannot be applied without disclosed revenue figures.\n\nThe two applicable methods yield a triangulated range of $145M (low) to $4.0B (high), with a median of $1.8B. The substantial spread reflects divergent signals: stage-progression favors a more conservative $171M valuation, while peer comparables suggest meaningfully higher value depending on clinical stage, IP position, and funding trajectory. Key uncertainties include the target's clinical progress versus peer cohorts, patent estate strength, and regulatory pathway clarity\u2014factors driving the wide peer valuation dispersion.",
