      "narrative": "Pivot Bio is a Series C-stage robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $920.9M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of nine private peers and one public company in the robotics and manufacturing sector, including later-stage companies like Exotec ($2.0B, Series D) and Hadrian ($1.6B, Series D), as well as adjacent-stage peers including Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B, Series B) and Dexterity ($1.6B, Series B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression method uses total capital raised ($921M) as a baseline proxy and applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical for Series C progression, yielding an implied valuation of $1.6B. The peer-median method analyzes a filtered set of seven same-sector and same/adjacent-stage companies, generating a median valuation of $1.6B with a range spanning $1.0B to $2.0B. Both approaches converge on the same point estimate.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $1.3B to $1.9B, with a median of $1.6B. The concentration of peer comps around $1.6B\u2013$2.0B and consistency between methodologies suggest limited downside risk. Key uncertainties include stage timing relative to peers (several comparable companies occupy Series B or Series D positions) and the sparse public comp set (n=1), which limits cross-sector benchmarking.",
