      "narrative": "Loyal is a Series C biotech company founded by Celine Halioua that has raised $250M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer universe of 3 public companies (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private-stage biotech firms, with 3 same-sector, same-stage private comparables used for direct benchmarking.\n\nTwo triangulation methods applied here. Stage-progression analysis uses the $250M total raised as a proxy base and applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement, yielding $425M. Peer-median anchoring draws on 3 same-sector Series C companies\u2014Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B), Chai Discovery ($3.8B), and New Limit ($3.1B)\u2014producing a median valuation of $3.8B. Public-comp P/S anchoring is inapplicable due to lack of disclosed revenue. The peer range spans $3.1B to $10.3B, reflecting material dispersion within the cohort.\n\nTriangulation across these two methods supports a valuation range of $361M (low) to $4.4B (high), with a median of $2.1B. The wide spread reflects the substantial variance in comparable company valuations and the sensitivity of stage-progression methods to growth assumptions. Key uncertainties include the lack of disclosed revenue (preventing P/S validation), the small peer sample size, and the significant outlier valuation of Colossal Biosciences relative to the other two comparables.",
