      "narrative": "Cradle is a Series B biotech company that has raised $102.7M to date across its founding team of five. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable set of 11 private and public companies in the Biotech & Health sector, including four same-stage or adjacent-stage private peers (Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, New Limit, and Eikon Therapeutics) valued between $539M and $10.3B, plus three public biotech reference companies (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. The stage-progression method, using total raised ($103M) as a proxy base and applying a 1.9x Series B-to-next-stage multiplier, implies a valuation of $195M. The peer-median method anchors to the median valuation of the four private comparables at $3.5B, reflecting a wide range from $539M (Eikon Therapeutics) to $10.3B (Colossal Biosciences). Public-comp anchoring via price-to-sales multiples (9.2x median across the three public tickers) cannot be applied without disclosed revenue figures.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $166M (low) to $4.0B (high), with a median of $1.8B. The wide dispersion reflects meaningful uncertainty around Cradle's stage maturity, technology risk, and go-to-market trajectory relative to heterogeneous peers. Stage-progression suggests a floor near $195M; peer medians suggest $1.8B\u2013$3.5B is defensible given comparable valuations at adjacent stages.",
