      "narrative": "Ampaire is a Series A\u2013stage Space & Aerospace company that has raised $74M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 3 private peers in the same sector at comparable or adjacent stages (Cowboy Space Corporation at $2.0B Series B, Aalyria at $1.3B Series B, and Starcloud at $1.1B Seed).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier to the $74M total raised, yielding an implied valuation of $148M. Peer-median analysis across the 3 private comparables produces a median valuation of $1.3B, with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied due to absence of disclosed revenue for the target. The two applicable methods produce a wide spread, reflecting material uncertainty around Ampaire's position within the frontier-aerospace market.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a range of $126M (low) to $1.5B (high), with a median of $724M. The extreme width of this range reflects tension between the stage-progression method, which anchors to capital raised, and peer-median analysis, which reflects post-money valuations of more mature, funded peers. Key uncertainties include whether Ampaire's technology risk and revenue trajectory align with the Series B\u2013stage peers or represent earlier-stage risk, and whether the peer set adequately reflects market conditions at time of Ampaire's next financing.",
