      "narrative": "Vantage Robotics is a Series C defense and security company founded by Tobin Fisher and Joe van Niekerk. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 12 same-sector and adjacent-stage peers, comprising 2 public companies (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 10 private entities including Helsing, Saronic, Quantum-Systems, Chaos Industries, and Dream Security.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using $46M in total raised as a proxy base value, applies a 1.7x multiplier typical of Series C advancement, yielding $78M. The peer-median method references 12 comparable companies in Defense & Security across Series B through Series D stages. The peer sample spans $300M to $18.0B in valuation, with Helsing and Saronic at the upper end ($18.0B and $9.2B respectively) and a median of $2.3B. This wide dispersion reflects significant heterogeneity in stage, technology maturity, and capital intensity within the sector.\n\nTriangulation of these two approaches produces a valuation range of $66M (low) to $2.7B (high), with a median of $1.2B. The wide range reflects tension between the stage-progression method\u2014anchored to recent fundraising\u2014and the peer-median method, which captures a mature, late-stage cohort. Key uncertainties include the target's revenue traction, customer concentration, and technology differentiation relative to better-capitalized competitors such as Anduril Industries and Shield AI.",
