      "narrative": "Burro is a Series C robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $44.8M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparison universe of nine private robotics firms at similar or adjacent stages, plus one public comparable (277810.KQ).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression method uses total capital raised ($45M) as a proxy for current implied value and applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement, yielding $76M. The peer-median method examines seven same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private comparables\u2014including Exotec ($2.0B Series D), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B Series B), Dexterity and Hadrian (each $1.6B), and others\u2014producing a median valuation of $1.6B against a range of $1.0B to $2.0B.\n\nThese methods produce a wide triangulated range: $65M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $863M. The disparity reflects genuine uncertainty around Burro's stage positioning relative to the peer set. The stage-progression result assumes conservative capital-efficiency extrapolation, while the peer median reflects comparables that may have achieved greater scale or revenue traction. Key uncertainties include Burro's current revenue run-rate, customer concentration, and capital efficiency relative to named peers. A median estimate near $863M is supportable but contingent on validation that Burro's operational metrics align with higher-valued Series B/D stage peers rather than early-stage benchmarks.",
