      "narrative": "Corvus Robotics is a Series C-stage robotics and manufacturing company founded by Jackie Wu and Mohammed Kabir, having raised $28.2M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 9 private peers and 1 public company in the robotics sector, including same and adjacent-stage companies such as Exotec (Series D, $2.0B), Bedrock Robotics (Series B, $1.8B), Dexterity (Series B, $1.6B), and Hadrian (Series D, $1.6B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised as a proxy baseline, applies a typical 1.7x Series C step-up multiplier to the $28.2M raised, implying a valuation of $48M. Peer-median analysis across 7 same-sector and same/adjacent-stage comparables yields a median valuation of $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.0B to $2.0B. The peer set skews toward later-stage funding rounds and demonstrates significant valuation dispersion.\n\nThe triangulated analysis produces a wide range from $41M to $1.9B, with a median of $849M. This spread reflects material uncertainty around Corvus' relative positioning within its peer cohort\u2014specifically, the company's product maturity, customer traction, and unit economics relative to Series B and D-stage peers. Resolution of these factors will be critical to narrowing the valuation band materially.",
