      "narrative": "Beacon AI is a Series A space & aerospace company founded by Matt Cox and Avinash Nair that has raised $26.4M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer set spanning 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private companies including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, ICEYE, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A advancement, yielding $53M based on the $26.4M raised proxy. Peer-median analysis across 3 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage companies (Cowboy Space Corporation at $2.0B, Aalyria at $1.3B, and Starcloud at $1.1B) produces a median of $1.3B, with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B. Public-comp anchoring via Space & Aerospace P/S multiple (27.4x median across 6 tickers) is not applicable due to the absence of target revenue disclosure.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $45M (low) to $1.5B (high), with a median of $676M. The wide spread reflects material methodological tension: stage-progression conservatism versus peer-median elevation driven by strong private-market valuations in the space sector. Key uncertainties include the comparability of peer stage disparity (Cowboy Space at Series B versus Starcloud at Seed) and whether private-market multiples in frontier aerospace sustain at Beacon's scale.",
