      "narrative": "Orchard Robotics, a Series A robotics and manufacturing company led by founder Charlie Wu, has raised $25.8M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of nine private robotics firms and one public comparable, spanning seed through Series B stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, using the $25.8M raised as a valuation proxy, yielding $52M. Peer-median analysis references four same-sector comparables\u2014Generalist AI ($2.0B, Series B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B, Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B, Series B), and Walden Robotics ($1.1B, Seed)\u2014producing a median valuation of $1.7B with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $44M (low) to $2.0B (high), with a median of $876M. The wide dispersion reflects material stage discrepancy within the peer set: two comparables are at Series B, one at Seed, and one unspecified. Key uncertainties include capital efficiency relative to more advanced peers, progress toward commercial deployment, and whether Orchard's specific robotics application commands premium or discount multiples within the sector. A more tightly staged peer set would materially narrow the range.",
