      "narrative": "Electric Sheep, a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Gunjit Singh, Jarrett Herold, and Naganand Murty, has raised $25.5M to date. The peer universe consists of nine comparable companies\u2014one public (277810.KQ) and eight private firms including Divergent, Exotec, Locus Robotics, Generalist AI, and Bedrock Robotics\u2014operating in the same sector and stage band.\n\nTwo triangulation methods apply here. Stage-progression analysis uses the $25.5M raised as a valuation proxy and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A-to-next-stage advancement, yielding $51M. Peer-median analysis benchmarks Electric Sheep against four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables: Generalist AI ($2.0B Series B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B Series B), and Walden Robotics ($1.1B Seed). The median across this set is $1.7B, with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $43M (low) to $2.0B (high), with a median of $876M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around Electric Sheep's position within the peer set: the stage-progression method assumes minimal value creation since funding, while the peer-median method assumes near-parity with more-advanced Series B cohorts. Key uncertainties include whether Electric Sheep's technology and market traction justify peer-level valuations at an earlier stage, and the relevance of the single public comparable.",
