      "narrative": "Podium Automation is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Jamie Niu Serota and Jacob Buser that has raised $23M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 9 private companies and 1 public company in the robotics and manufacturing sector, including four direct peers: Generalist AI ($2.0B, Series B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B, Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B, Series B), and Walden Robotics ($1.1B, Seed).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using the $23M raised as a value proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, implies a valuation of $46M. Peer-median analysis across the four same-sector comparables yields a median valuation of $1.7B, with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B. The stark divergence reflects the substantial stage gap: three of the four peers are in Series B, while Podium remains in Series A.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a range of $39M (low) to $2.0B (high), with a median of $873M. The wide range reflects genuine uncertainty around near-term capital efficiency and market traction relative to later-stage peers. Key variables for narrowing this band include Series A funding trajectory, customer acquisition metrics, and whether the company's technical capabilities command stage-appropriate premium valuation within the sector.",
