      "narrative": "zeroRISC is a Seed-stage semiconductor company that has raised $15M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a universe of 3 public semiconductor comparables (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private peers in chips and semiconductors, with particular relevance to Series A stage companies including SambaNova Systems, Rebellions, and d-Matrix.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised as a proxy, applies a typical 2.5x multiplier from Seed to next-stage entry, implying a valuation of $38M. Peer-median anchoring across the three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yields a median valuation of $2.3B, with a range spanning $2.0B (d-Matrix) to $11.0B (SambaNova Systems). Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (median 20.5x across the three public tickers) cannot be applied due to absence of revenue disclosure. The triangulated analysis across applicable methods supports a range of $32M (low) to $2.7B (high), with a median of $1.2B. Key uncertainties include the wide dispersion in peer valuations\u2014particularly SambaNova's $11B outlier\u2014and zeroRISC's undisclosed product maturity relative to Series A stage peers. Revenue trajectory and technical differentiation will be material to positioning within this band.",
