      "narrative": "Aon3D is a Series C robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $14.4M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of nine comparable companies\u2014one public and eight private\u2014spanning the same sector and stage range, including Series B and D-stage reference points such as Exotec ($2.0B), Dexterity ($1.6B), and Hadrian ($1.6B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression approach, anchoring to $14M in total raised and applying a 1.7x multiplier typical of Series C advancement, implies a valuation of $24M. The peer-median method, based on seven same-sector and same/adjacent-stage comparables, yields a median valuation of $1.6B with a range of $1.0B to $2.0B. This disparity reflects significant heterogeneity within the robotics cohort, where stage timing and market positioning drive material valuation variance.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a range of $21M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $837M. The wide band reflects inherent tension between two methodologies: stage-progression produces a conservative floor based on capital deployed, while peer-median captures market sentiment toward robotics ventures but introduces noise from timing and company-specific factors. Key uncertainties include capital deployment velocity, technology differentiation relative to peers, and nearness to Series D or equivalent inflection point.",
