      "narrative": "Specter Aerospace is a Series C-stage space and aerospace company founded by Felipe Gomez del Campo and Drew Weibel. The firm has raised $14.4M to date. Our analysis applies two triangulation methods against a comparable universe of 6 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private firms (Sierra Space, Apex Space, Cowboy Space Corporation, Varda Space Industries, Aalyria, and one additional peer) and 5 public Space & Aerospace comps (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL).\n\nStage-progression methodology, applying a 1.7x multiplier typical for Series C advancement to the $14.4M raised proxy, implies a $24M valuation. Peer-median analysis across the 6 private comparables yields a $1.8B midpoint, with a range spanning $1.1B to $8.0B. The public-comp P/S approach (median 27.4x across 5 tickers) was not applicable due to absence of target revenue disclosure. These two applicable methods triangulate to a range of $21M (low) to $2.1B (high), with a median of $907M.\n\nThe wide dispersion ($21M to $2.1B) reflects material uncertainty in early-stage aerospace valuation. Stage-progression anchors conservatively on capital deployed; peer medians capture market valuations but show wide dispersion driven by company-specific factors and funding availability in the sector. Key uncertainties include Specter's specific technology differentiation, revenue traction, and capital efficiency relative to peers.",
