      "narrative": "Pryzm is a Seed-stage Defense & Security company that has raised $14.2M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 10 private and 2 public peers in the same sector and stage cohort, including UFORCE, Anduril Industries, Helsing, Shield AI, and Saronic as key private benchmarks.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised as a proxy for current value, applies a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage advancement, yielding $36M. Peer-median analysis examines five same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables: UFORCE ($1.0B, Seed), Castelion ($1.0B, Series A), Stark Defence ($4.0B, Series A), Singularity ($400M, Series A), and NODA AI ($125M, Series A). The median across this cohort is $1.0B, with a range spanning $125M to $4.0B.\n\nTriangulating these two methods produces a valuation range of $30M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $518M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty in peer comparability: the stage-progression method anchors conservatively on capital raised, while the peer-median approach captures a heterogeneous set including later-stage rounds that command substantial premiums. Key uncertainties include revenue traction, customer concentration, and technology differentiation relative to the peer set.",
