      "narrative": "Laminar is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Annie Lu and David Lu, having raised $12.4M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of nine private peers and one public comparable, spanning the robotics and manufacturing sector at similar and adjacent stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis uses total raised as a proxy base of $12M and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A advancement, implying a valuation of $25M. Peer-median analysis examines four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Generalist AI ($2.0B Series B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B Series B), and Walden Robotics ($1.1B Seed)\u2014yielding a median of $1.7B with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B.\n\nThe two methods produce a wide triangulated range of $21M (low) to $2.0B (high), with a median of $862M. The disparity reflects fundamental uncertainty: stage-progression anchored to early capital deployment versus peer-median anchored to later-stage comparable valuations. The peer set skews toward Series B and later stages, which may overstate fair value for a Series A company. Key uncertainties include capital efficiency relative to peers, product-market validation metrics, and whether the peer cohort represents an appropriate comparable set for a nascent Series A business.",
