      "narrative": "Danti is a seed-stage Space & Aerospace company founded by Jesse Kallman and Martice Nicks III that has raised $10.9M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 6 public Space & Aerospace companies (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, and ICEYE.\n\nOf three potential valuation methods, only stage-progression proved applicable. Using total capital raised ($11M) as a proxy for seed-stage valuation and applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of seed-to-next-round progression yields an implied valuation of $27M. Public-comp anchoring could not be deployed due to the absence of target revenue data\u2014a standard limitation in early-stage private company analysis. Peer-median analysis was inapplicable: while 14 same-sector peers exist, the narrow filters (same-stage, adjacent-stage, similar-tier) returned fewer than the minimum 3 datapoints required for meaningful statistical reliability, and sector-wide medians would introduce material distortion bias.\n\nThe triangulation, constrained to a single methodology, supports a valuation range of $23M to $31M, with a median estimate of $27M. Key uncertainties include the lack of revenue visibility, absence of comparable seed-stage transactions in the narrow Space & Aerospace subset, and reliance on a single step-up multiplier. Widening the range or anchoring to broader peer sets would require either revenue disclosure or documented transaction data from stage-equivalent peers.",
