      "narrative": "Stratum AI is a seed-stage climate and energy company founded by Daniel Mogilny and Farzi Yusufali. The target operates within a frontier-tech sector represented by a limited peer universe: one public company (LNZA) and eight private firms including Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Enovix. The company has raised $400K to date.\n\nValuation analysis relies on stage-progression methodology, which is applicable given the seed stage and capital history. Using total raised ($400K) as a baseline proxy and applying a typical 2.5x multiplier for progression from seed to next stage yields an implied valuation of $1M. A peer-median approach was not viable; although eight same-sector comparables exist, insufficient data points met narrow screening criteria (same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar-tier valuation), and a broad sector median would introduce unwarranted noise.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $850K to $1.15M, with a median point of $1M. This narrow range reflects reliance on a single method rather than convergence across multiple approaches. Key uncertainties include the absence of traction-based metrics (revenue, user growth, or technical milestones), limited private peer comparability at the seed stage, and the nascent nature of frontier-energy valuations, where traditional venture benchmarks may not fully capture risk or market potential. Additional data on burn rate and runway would sharpen conviction in this range.",
